    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    # Milestone 4 part 2 P1 gate.log (specs/0031-release-metadata.md, "P1:
    # the CHANGELOG, the doc comment, the licence texts", "Phases" and
    # "Planning rulings during P1" rulings 1 to 5; the specs/0001 rules for
    # every phase): the environment line first (the root's mount propagation
    # and the keepalive, each a check with a control), M4 part 1 P3's build
    # targets and the part 1 close-out's target root listed with their sizes
    # and pruned, the spec pinned by the hash of its committed blob, planning's
    # working copy printed, the full gate on the phase's main-tree target
    # directory with the doc directory removed before it, the phase's four
    # commits by role (the doc commit, then the CHANGELOG, the doc comment and
    # the package files, the last the phase commit, over part 1's close-out
    # record commit) and by the paths each touches, every commit planning docs
    # alone or code alone with the doc commit first, each commit message's form
    # and the count rule, the doc commit's three files against the hashes of
    # its blobs and against the hashes its own message gives, each commit's
    # diff hashed, each file's mode kept and no added file executable, each
    # code commit's files with the status git gives each, the tree at the phase
    # commit equal to the base's outside the phase's eight files, the doc
    # comment's diff doc lines alone, the manifest gaining the readme line alone
    # after publish = false, the licence copies the root's blobs, no other Rust
    # source, no lock, tool or script changed, README.md not in the range, the
    # crate's messages unchanged, the gate files checked against the diff and
    # none changed, the scripts parsed and compiled, the new and modified files
    # scored, the public fn and const first lines the base's, the consumer crate
    # of part 6 P3 naming the call with the features off, comments alone, copy
    # alone and the two together, clippy and doc with the features off, copy
    # alone, comments alone, the two together and every feature, each doc build
    # after its directory is removed and asserting rustdoc ran, the index's item
    # links counted with the section anchors excluded, clippy over the probe
    # crate's feature sets, the crate's tests with the features off, comments
    # alone, copy alone, copy with comments and every feature on both targets,
    # no test file in the range and the test names of the whole tree the base's,
    # the four DEBUG binary hashes and their copies kept, this script's own
    # stderr counted, and the working tree's status, planning's uncommitted spec
    # allowed.
    #
    # Usage: PRUNE_PREVIOUS=list|yes m4p2-p1-gate.sh <phase commit> > <file outside
    # the tree>; the caller moves the output to records/logs/m4p2-p1/gate.log. The log prints its own
    # invocation, and every environment input it reads on a labelled line after it.
    #
    # This is a FILE, not an inline block, so "$0" names it and the log prints the
    # script rather than the shell binary.
    #
    # Its own text is committed inside the log, so it holds no office file name, no
    # path shape and no address: the office regex is read from check.sh, the
    # pre-P6d path forms are read from git, and every control fixture is assembled
    # at run time from pieces (specs/0001-bootstrap.md, as in every earlier gate log).
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 4c P1 from part 4b P4's gate script (at the phase
    # commit 5854e34, printed in records/logs/m2p4b-p4/gate.log; its change list
    # A10 to H10 is there), generated by <phase>/gen/gate.py, which asserts each
    # replacement once, and grepped for P4's names, subjects, typed lists, hashes
    # and the tokens m2p4b-p4, P4, 2b4afb62, 93150aa7, the probe and the
    # catalogue commit in every form; the manifest, public-list and package-tests
    # checks follow part 4b P1's gate (printed in records/logs/m2p4b-p1/gate.log,
    # its changes C7, D7, E7 and F7), the feature being new here as rules was
    # there. What differs, and why:
    #  A11. The phase is part 4c P1: the log directory records/logs/m2p4c-p1; the
    #       script in <scripts> on the disk, beside <phase>/out (this script's
    #       stderr) and <build> (<phase>/gate). The base is part 4b's close-out
    #       record commit ("M2 part 4b close-out record:"); the doc commit and the
    #       three code commits by their full subjects, all beginning "M2 part 4c
    #       P1: ", the roles read back to <phase commit>~4. A rerun line names the
    #       superseded directory as <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p4c-p1/superseded.
    #  B11. The spec is specs/0021, pinned by the hash of its COMMITTED blob
    #       (b96f97ac..., planning's word), at the doc commit and at the phase
    #       commit; the working tree's copy holds planning's uncommitted rulings
    #       during P1 and is printed, not pinned. The doc commit's three files
    #       (ROADMAP.md 85ba5204..., specs/0020 5fc132f2..., specs/0021
    #       b96f97ac...) against the hashes planning's message gave, typed here;
    #       the path-absent control names specs/0021 at the base, which lacks it.
    #  C11. The areas: code commit 1 (specs/0020 P4 verification ruling 6's
    #       carry, with P1 ruling 1's test) holds to package.rs and
    #       package/tests/conditional.rs, every package.rs line it adds or removes
    #       a //! line, the test file losing no line and gaining the compose test
    #       the base lacks; code commit 2 (the crate) to the crate's manifest,
    #       lib.rs, package.rs, package/tests.rs and package/tests/tables.rs; code
    #       commit 3 (the tool) to the tool's manifest, main.rs and
    #       tests/null_rewrite.rs. The styles module is untouched.
    #  D11. Manifests, as part 4b P1's D7: the crate's, code commit 2's, whose one
    #       non-comment change is the feature tables with no dependency; the
    #       tool's, code commit 3's, whose one non-comment change is tables added
    #       to its emend features; no Cargo.lock.
    #  E11. The public first lines: with the feature tables off the list is the
    #       base's, line for line; with it on it adds exactly add_table and
    #       tables, and those two alone carry the tables cfg line; the rules and
    #       metadata items are the base's; the rowcol items are the base's four
    #       calls, and TABLE and PIVOT_TABLE carry the cfg line naming rowcol or
    #       tables (the shared readers, P1's design). The consumer crate names the
    #       six items tables gates: the two calls and Table, TableEntry,
    #       TableStyle and TableStyleInfo.
    #  F11. The base's tests: none gone and none edited; package/tests.rs gains
    #       exactly the tables module's two declaration lines.
    #  G11. Clippy and doc with the feature tables off and on and every feature
    #       on; the crate's tests with tables off and on on both targets. The
    #       probe crate's clippy keeps part 4b P4's feature sets (this phase
    #       touches no probe).
    #  H11. The status patterns name this phase's log directory, its record stems
    #       records/m2p4c-p1- and records/m2p4c-open-, and planning's uncommitted
    #       specs/0021, each with a control; no size record in this phase.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 4c P2 from part 4c P1's gate script (at the phase
    # commit 40ae039, printed in records/logs/m2p4c-p1/gate.log; its change list
    # A11 to H11 is above), generated by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p4c-p2/gen/
    # gate.py, which asserts each replacement once, and grepped for P1's names,
    # subjects, typed lists, hashes and the tokens m2p4c-p1, 4c P1, b96f97ac,
    # 5fc132f2, 85ba5204 and the manifests in every form. What differs, and why:
    #  A12. The phase is part 4c P2: the log directory records/logs/m2p4c-p2; the
    #       script in <scripts> on the disk, beside <phase>/out and <build>
    #       (<phase>/gate). The base is part 4c P1's record commit ("M2 part 4c
    #       P1 record:"); the doc commit and the three code commits by their
    #       full subjects, all beginning "M2 part 4c P2: ", the roles read back to
    #       <phase commit>~4. A rerun line names the superseded directory as
    #       <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p4c-p2/superseded.
    #  B12. The spec is specs/0021, pinned by the hash of its COMMITTED blob
    #       (3bea86d5..., planning's word), at the doc commit and at the phase
    #       commit. The doc commit's two files (ROADMAP.md dc334d27...,
    #       specs/0021 3bea86d5...) against the hashes planning's message gave,
    #       typed here; the path-absent control names a file the base lacks.
    #  C12. The areas: code commit 1 (the P1 verification carry, specs/0021 P1
    #       verification ruling 5) holds to package.rs, package/tests/tables.rs
    #       and package/tests/names.rs, and adds the shared helper names_a_cell
    #       the base lacks, used by both name rules, with add_table's entry-name
    #       sentence brought to P1 ruling 6; code commit 2 (the removal) to
    #       package.rs and package/tests/tables.rs; code commit 3 (the tool) to
    #       the tool's main.rs and tests/null_rewrite.rs.
    #  D12. No manifest and no Cargo.lock in the phase diff: the feature and the
    #       tool's features are part 4c P1's.
    #  E12. The public first lines: with the feature tables off the list is the
    #       base's with it off, line for line; with it on it adds exactly
    #       add_table, remove_table and tables, those three alone carrying the
    #       tables cfg line, and adds to the base's with it on remove_table
    #       alone; the rowcol and shared items are the base's. The consumer crate
    #       names the seven items tables gates.
    #  F12. The base's tests: none gone; the edits are exactly the carry's
    #       (P1 verification ruling 5: the call-time table's two R1C1 rows and
    #       its length, the header-cell test's third table, the defined-name
    #       rule's Table1 and xyz1) and the tool test's two line keys and its
    #       comment, each line listed and compared; package/tests.rs unchanged.
    #  G12. As G11.
    #  H12. The status patterns name this phase's log directory and its record
    #       stems records/m2p4c-p2- and records/m2p4c-open-, and planning's
