    #       prefix_len" lines, each with "#[cfg(test)]" on the line before (the
    #       base held one pub fn: the control). Every changed Rust source lies
    #       under crates/emend/src or tools/emend-copy/src (a planted path
    #       elsewhere: the control); no Cargo.toml and no Cargo.lock changes,
    #       each with a control on a commit that did; README.md not in the range
    #       (P1's form). The crate's messages are the base's, as a set.
    #  F43. No gate file changed: P1's listing form.
    #  G43. The modes as P1's; no file is added.
    #  H43. No Python script is in the phase diff.
    #  I43. The tests: four test files are in the phase diff; no test of the
    #       base is gone; every line removed from or added to a base test's body
    #       is either a comment or the rename of its counterpart (the removed
    #       non-comment lines with the old names replaced by the new, in order,
    #       are the added non-comment lines); and the names of every #[test] fn
    #       in every Rust file of the tree are the base's, as a sorted list. P1's
    #       "package/tests.rs not changed" is replaced: the rename edits it.
    #  J43. The status patterns name this phase's log directory and planning's
    #       uncommitted specs/0030, each with a control.
    #  K43. The DEBUG binaries and their copies stay as the carried form.
    #  L43. The public fn and const first lines: the phase commit's list is the
    #       base's but for the lines the renames and the hide change. Lost from
    #       the base's: the shared_string_items, defaults and prefix_len first
    #       lines; added: the first two with the old names replaced by the new.
    #       Every other cfg line's items are the base's, as before.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M4 part 1 P3 from M4 part 1 P2's gate script (at the phase
    # commit 8902f87, printed in records/logs/m4p1-p2/gate.log; its change list
    # A43 to L43 is above), generated by
    # <home>/.cache/emend-build/m4p1-p3/gen/gate.py, which asserts each
    # replacement's count, and grepped for P2's names, subjects, hashes and the
    # tokens 04b7070, 828b7dc, the P2 spec pin and m4p1-p2-gate over the
    # header's paragraph and usage lines and the whole body. What differs, and
    # why:
    #  A44. The phase is Milestone 4 part 1 P3 (specs/0030-carries-and-api-
    #       changes.md, "P3: the samples, the size and the listing"): the log
    #       directory records/logs/m4p1-p3; the script in <scripts> beside
    #       <phase>/out and <build>. The base is P2's record commit ("M4 part 1
    #       P2 record:"); the phase holds one commit, the doc commit, which is
    #       the phase commit (no code change: FACTS.md and the spec's P3), found
    #       by its full subject, beginning "M4 part 1 P3: ", its parent the base.
    #       The range is planning docs alone: every commit a doc commit, at
    #       least one, no code commit (structure_sound gives way to
    #       docs_only_sound, with controls that refuse a code commit, a mixed
    #       commit and an empty range). The code-commit control of
    #       commit_class names its commit by what it did: the last commit that
    #       modified crates/emend/src/archive.rs (P2's phase commit, outside
    #       the range).
    #  B44. The environment line stands as P1's change B37 wrote it.
    #  C44. The prune (specs/0001, one target root per phase; FACTS.md, as
    #       P2's gate named P1's): under <home>/.cache/emend-build/m4p1-p2, the
    #       five names dry-gate, gate, negative, test and the whole target root,
    #       each printed with du -sb before, removed by rm -r without -f,
    #       checked gone; every other name the directory holds is checked still
    #       there, dry-logs among them (P2 verification ruling 4 cites the dry
    #       run), and every name is in exactly one of the two sets.
    #  D44. The spec is specs/0030, pinned by the hash of its COMMITTED blob at
    #       this phase's doc commit (99f64b5f..., read from the blob when the
    #       generator ran and checked against the 16-digit prefix planning's
    #       brief gave) at the phase commit; the working tree's copy, which
    #       carries planning's rulings during P3 uncommitted, is printed, not
    #       pinned, and so is ROADMAP.md's. The doc commit's two files, both
    #       modified, against the hashes of its blobs at the doc commit and at
    #       the phase commit, each refused at the base, which holds P2's copies;
    #       the doc commit's message read for its "<path> sha256 <hash>" pairs;
    #       the lines it removes printed.
    #  E44. The areas: the tree at the phase commit equals P2's phase commit
    #       (found by its subject) for every path outside specs/, ROADMAP.md and
    #       records/ (git diff --quiet, with a control: the same check refuses
    #       P2's phase commit's parent, whose archive.rs differs); no Rust
    #       source, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock or file under scripts/ in the range,
    #       each with a control on a commit that did change one; README.md not
    #       in the range (P1's form). P2's per-commit areas, declarations,
    #       re-exports and prefix_len checks are dropped: P2 proved them and the
    #       tree equality carries them.
    #  F44. No gate file changed: P1's listing form.
    #  G44. The modes as P1's; no file is added.
    #  H44. No Python script is in the phase diff (P2's form).
    #  I44. The tests: no test file is in the phase diff (a planted list of one
    #       is the control); no base test is edited or gone; the names of every
    #       #[test] fn in every Rust file of the tree are the base's, as a
    #       sorted list (P2's form).
    #  J44. The status patterns name this phase's log directory and planning's
    #       uncommitted specs/0030, each with a control.
    #  K44. The DEBUG binaries and their copies stay as the carried form.
    #  L44. The public fn and const first lines: the phase commit's list is the
    #       base's exactly, with a control one line short.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M4 part 2 P1 from M4 part 1 P3's gate script (at the phase
    # commit 669fa91, printed in records/logs/m4p1-p3/gate.log; its change list
    # A44 to L44 is above), generated by
    # <home>/.cache/emend-build/m4p2-p1/gen/gate.py, which asserts each
    # replacement's count, re-adds the code-commit handling of M4 part 1 P2's
    # gate script (printed in records/logs/m4p1-p2/gate.log), and greps for
    # P3's names, subjects, hashes and the tokens 669fa91, 84c40da, the P3 spec
    # pin and the P3 ROADMAP hash over the header's paragraph and usage lines
    # and the whole body. What differs, and why:
    #  A45. The phase is Milestone 4 part 2 P1 (specs/0031-release-metadata.md,
    #       "P1: the CHANGELOG, the doc comment, the licence texts"): the log
    #       directory records/logs/m4p2-p1. The base is M4 part 1's close-out
    #       record commit ("M4 part 1 close-out record:"); the phase holds four
    #       commits found by their full subjects, each beginning "M4 part 2 P1: ":
    #       the doc commit, then three code commits (the CHANGELOG, the
    #       crate-level doc comment, the README and the licence texts in the
    #       package), the last the phase commit, each the next one's parent and
    #       the doc commit's parent the base. docs_only_sound gives way to P2's
    #       structure_sound again (every commit docs alone or code alone, the
    #       range opening with a doc commit and holding code), with P2's
    #       controls; the code-commit control of commit_class names its commit
    #       by what it did: the commit in the range that modified
    #       crates/emend/src/lib.rs. The classifier reads CHANGELOG.md as code,
    #       not as planning docs.
    #  B45. The environment line stands as P1's change B37 wrote it.
    #  C45. The prune (specs/0001, one target root per phase; specs/0031
    #       "Phases"; specs/0030 close-out ruling 10): two directories, each
    #       with its own prune set and kept names, through one function: under
    #       <home>/.cache/emend-build/m4p1-p3 the four names dry-gate, gate, test
    #       and the whole target root; under <home>/.cache/emend-build/m4p1-close
    #       the target root alone. Each name printed with du -sb before, a total
    #       per directory, removed by rm -r without -f, checked gone; every
    #       other name each directory holds is checked still there (the
    #       close-out's gen.py, logs, check1 and superseded among them), and
    #       every name is in exactly one of its directory's two sets. The
    #       accounted_all control drops the first kept name.
    #  D45. The spec is specs/0031, pinned by the hash of its COMMITTED blob at
    #       this phase's doc commit (18cab49d..., read from the blob when the
    #       generator ran and checked against the 8-digit prefix planning's
    #       brief gave) at the phase commit; the working tree's copy, which
    #       carries planning's rulings during P1 uncommitted, is printed, not
    #       pinned, and so is ROADMAP.md's. The doc commit's three files
    #       (specs/0031 added, specs/0030 and ROADMAP.md modified) against the
    #       hashes of their blobs at the doc commit and at the phase commit,
    #       each checked against the 8-digit prefix of planning's brief and
    #       refused at the base, which lacks specs/0031 and holds part 1's
    #       copies of the other two; the doc commit's message read for its
    #       "<path> sha256 <hash>" pairs; the lines it removes printed. The
    #       prefix control on the pin refuses specs/0030's blob at the phase
    #       commit.
    #  E45. The areas: each code commit's files, with the status git gives
    #       each, are the ones FACTS.md gives (P2's form); the tree at the phase
    #       commit equals the base's for every path outside the phase's eight
    #       files (git diff --quiet with a pathspec, with a control that leaves
    #       lib.rs out of the exclusions); the doc comment commit's diff, and the
    #       range's diff of crates/emend/src, hold doc lines alone (every added
    #       or removed line starting //!), with a control on a planted code line;
    #       the manifest's diff over the range adds exactly the line
    #       readme = "../../README.md", removes none, and the line before it at
    #       the phase commit is publish = false, refused at the base; each
    #       licence copy's blob is the root file's blob at the phase commit,
    #       with a control pairing the MIT copy with the Apache text; no Rust
    #       source but lib.rs, no Cargo.lock, nothing under tools/ or scripts/
    #       in the range, each with a control on a commit that did change one;
    #       README.md not in the range (P1's form); the crate's messages as
    #       before.
    #  F45. No gate file changed: P1's listing form.
    #  G45. The modes as P1's; the added files (specs/0031, CHANGELOG.md and the
    #       two licence copies) checked not executable.
    #  H45. No Python script is in the phase diff (P2's form).
    #  I45. The tests stand as P3's change I44 wrote them: no test file in the
    #       phase diff, no base test edited or gone, the test names the base's.
    #  J45. The status patterns name this phase's log directory and planning's
    #       uncommitted specs/0031, each with a control.
    #  K45. The DEBUG binaries and their copies stay as the carried form.
    #  L45. The public fn and const first lines: the phase commit's list is the
    #       base's exactly (the range changes doc lines alone in lib.rs), with a
    #       control one line short.
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    SELF=$SELF_DIR/$(basename "$0")
    PHASE_DIR=$(dirname "$SELF_DIR")
    # specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7: this script's own standard error, kept and counted at the end.
    mkdir -p "$PHASE_DIR/out" || exit 2
    ERR=$PHASE_DIR/out/gate.stderr
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    # Header change 1, kept: the build directory is on the disk, not in /tmp; a
    # dry run names another with GATE_BUILD_ROOT (changes A35 and A36).
    BUILD_ROOT=${GATE_BUILD_ROOT:-$PHASE_DIR/gate}
    # Change J35 (b) and K35: the phase's target root (ruling 8), one
    # subdirectory per source tree (ruling 10 of P3): <repo>'s builds in main,
    # the consumer crate's in consumer.
    SHARED_TARGET=$PHASE_DIR/target
    MAIN_TARGET=$SHARED_TARGET/main
    CONSUMER_TARGET=$SHARED_TARGET/consumer
    mkdir -p "$BUILD_ROOT" "$MAIN_TARGET" "$CONSUMER_TARGET" || exit 2
    export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$MAIN_TARGET
    # Change J35 (a): list or yes, nothing else.
    PRUNE_PREVIOUS=${PRUNE_PREVIOUS:-}
    case $PRUNE_PREVIOUS in list | yes) ;; *) echo "PRUNE_PREVIOUS is list or yes" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    # Change C45: M4 part 1 P3's directory and the part 1 close-out's.
    PREV_P3=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m4p1-p3
    PREV_CLOSE=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m4p1-close
    W=$(mktemp -d)
    # Change A24 (A22's form): the consumer crate's directory is made by this
    # run, under <build>, and removed by it at the end; the scrub writes it
    # <build>/consumer.
    CONSUMER=$(mktemp -d "$BUILD_ROOT/consumer.XXXXXX") || exit 2
    # Every printed line passes through this scrub: the repository first, since it
    # lies inside the home directory, then the deeper directories before the
    # shallower ones.
    scrub() {
      sed -E -e "s#$MAIN([^-A-Za-z0-9_.]|\$)#<repo>\\1#g" -e "s#$W#<scratch>/w#g" -e "s#$CONSUMER#<build>/consumer#g" -e "s#$SHARED_TARGET#<target>#g" -e "s#$BUILD_ROOT#<build>#g" \
        -e "s#$SELF_DIR#<scripts>#g" -e "s#$PHASE_DIR#<phase>#g" -e "s#$HOME#<home>#g"
    }
    exec 3>&1
    exec > >(scrub >&3)
    SCRUB_PID=$!
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    # Change C3: the library at the phase commit, not the main tree's file.
    git show "$C:scripts/counting.sh" >"$W/counting.sh" || exit 2
    . "$W/counting.sh"
    
    trap 'rm -rf "${W:?}" "${CONSUMER:?}"' EXIT INT TERM HUP
    fail=0
    note() { echo "  $1: $2"; [ "$2" = as-expected ] || fail=1; }
    is() { if "$@"; then echo as-expected; else echo UNEXPECTED; fi; }
    # For a control that must FAIL. `is ! f x` cannot express it: `!` is a shell
    # keyword, so "$@" would try to run a command named "!" and the helper would
    # print UNEXPECTED whatever f did.
    isnot() { if "$@"; then echo UNEXPECTED; else echo as-expected; fi; }
    ctl() {
      local label=$1 want=$2 n r
      shift 2
      n=$("$@")
      r=$([ "$n" = "$want" ] && echo as-expected || echo UNEXPECTED)
      echo "  control $label count=$n expected=$want: $r"
      [ "$r" = as-expected ] || fail=1
    }
    
    # specs/0001-bootstrap.md, "Rules for every phase" (M1 part 3 P1 ruling 11):
    # the phase commit is GIVEN to the script and compared with git rev-parse
    # HEAD before the run, with a control that refuses a fabricated commit.
    HEAD_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    full_sha() {
      printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'
    }
    is_head() { full_sha "$1" && [ "$1" = "$HEAD_SHA" ]; }
    not_head() { if is_head "$1"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    echo "invocation: bash <scripts>/$(basename "$0") $*"
    echo "about: M4 part 2 P1 phase commits, last is $C; HEAD at run: $HEAD_SHA"
    # Change J4: every environment input this script reads, on a labelled line.
    echo "input (environment) RERUN_NOTE: $([ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ] && echo "set; its text is the rerun line below" || echo unset)"
    echo "input (environment) RERUN_FILES: ${RERUN_FILES:-unset}"
    echo "input (environment) ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo set || echo unset)"
    echo "input (environment) HOME: $([ -n "${HOME:-}" ] && echo "set; the scrub writes it <home>" || echo unset)"
    echo "input (environment) PRUNE_PREVIOUS: $PRUNE_PREVIOUS (specs/0001, one target root per phase; changes J35 and C45)"
    echo "input (environment) GATE_BUILD_ROOT: ${GATE_BUILD_ROOT:+set; the build directory below is it}${GATE_BUILD_ROOT:-unset, so <build> is <phase>/gate}"
    echo
    echo "## the environment line: the root's mount propagation and the keepalive (specs/0029 item 1 and \"Planning rulings during P1\", ruling 4 (i); specs/0001 \"Rules for every phase\"; change B37)"
    # podman's first call warns on the script's standard error when the root is
    # not a shared mount, and a session's logged runs die with an ssh drop unless
    # the host's scheduled task holds its keepalive; both are read here, before
    # anything else the log does, each checked with controls on the same check.
    echo "command: findmnt -no PROPAGATION /"
    PROPAGATION=$(findmnt -no PROPAGATION / </dev/null)
    echo "  the root's mount propagation: ${PROPAGATION:-nothing read}"
    prop_shared() { [ "$1" = shared ]; }
    note "the root's mount propagation is shared" "$(is prop_shared "$PROPAGATION")"
    note "control: the same check refuses private" "$(isnot prop_shared private)"
    note "control: the same check refuses an empty reading" "$(isnot prop_shared "")"
    # keep_count <pattern>: the processes whose whole command line matches the
    # anchored pattern, or "error" when pgrep fails (exit 2 or more); pgrep -c
    # prints 0 and exits 1 when none match.
    keep_count() {
      local n rc
      n=$(pgrep -fc -- "$1" </dev/null)
      rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -le 1 ]; then printf '%s' "$n"; else printf error; fi
    }
    KEEPALIVE_RE='^/usr/bin/sleep 2147483647$'
    echo "command: pgrep -fc -- '$KEEPALIVE_RE'"
    NKEEP=$(keep_count "$KEEPALIVE_RE")
    echo "  keepalive processes: $NKEEP"
    keep_one() { [ "$1" = 1 ]; }
    note "exactly one keepalive process is running" "$(is keep_one "$NKEEP")"
    note "control: the same check refuses 0" "$(isnot keep_one 0)"
    note "control: the same check refuses 2" "$(isnot keep_one 2)"
    note "control: the same check refuses error" "$(isnot keep_one error)"
    # The counting form on a process this script starts: a sleep with a duration
    # no other process uses, disowned so that its end prints no job notice on the
    # script's standard error, counted while it runs and after it is stopped.
    CTL_RE='^sleep 987654321$'
    sleep 987654321 </dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1 &
    CTL_PID=$!
    disown "$CTL_PID"
    k=0
    while [ "$(keep_count "$CTL_RE")" != 1 ] && [ "$k" -lt 50 ]; do sleep 0.1; k=$((k + 1)); done
    ctl "keep_count on the anchored command line of a sleep this script started" 1 keep_count "$CTL_RE"
    kill "$CTL_PID"
    k=0
    while [ "$(keep_count "$CTL_RE")" != 0 ] && [ "$k" -lt 50 ]; do sleep 0.1; k=$((k + 1)); done
    ctl "keep_count on the same line after this script stopped it" 0 keep_count "$CTL_RE"
    ctl "keep_count on a pattern no process matches" 0 keep_count '^no such command line here$'
    
    echo
    echo "## the three shape greps, over this script, before its log (specs/0001)"
    # specs/0001: the scan greps every printed script for three forbidden shapes,
    # and they run here first, over this script's own file, each with a positive
    # control through the same command form. The patterns and the fixture are
    # assembled from pieces at run time, so this script's text holds none.
    D='$'
    SHAPE_CHAIN="\\${D}\\((yn|is|isnot) .*(&&|\\|\\|)"
    SHAPE_BANG="\\${D}\\((yn|is|isnot) !"
    SHAPE_ASSIGN="\\${D}\\((yn|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
    SHAPE_DIR=$(mktemp -d)
    printf '%s\n' "x=${D}(is [ 1 ] && true)" "y=${D}(isnot ! true)" "z=${D}(yn N=1 true)" >"$SHAPE_DIR/fixture"
    echo "command: count_matches -E <shape> <this script>, and the same over a fixture holding one line of each shape"
    for shape in CHAIN BANG ASSIGN; do
      var=SHAPE_$shape
      n_self=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$SELF")
      n_fix=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$SHAPE_DIR/fixture")
      echo "  shape $shape: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
      SHAPE_RESULT_SELF=$n_self
      SHAPE_RESULT_FIX=$n_fix
      note "$shape: this script holds none" "$(is [ "$SHAPE_RESULT_SELF" = 0 ])"
      note "control: $shape: the same form finds the fixture's one line" "$(is [ "$SHAPE_RESULT_FIX" = 1 ])"
    done
    rm -rf "${SHAPE_DIR:?}"
    
    echo
    echo "## the previous phases' build targets, listed with their sizes and pruned (specs/0001 \"Rules for every phase\", one target root per phase; specs/0031 \"Phases\"; specs/0030 close-out ruling 10; changes J35 and C45)"
    # The standing rule: at a new phase's first gate that builds, the previous
    # phase's cargo target directories, run outputs and dry copies go, listed
    # with their sizes first, by rm -r without -f; never a name a committed log
    # or a record cites. The names are typed from each directory as it stands;
    # nothing outside the two directories is touched. Change C45: M4 part 1 P3's
    # four build and scratch names, its whole target root among them, and the
    # part 1 close-out's target root (specs/0031 "Phases"; specs/0030 close-out
    # ruling 10). Every other name stays: the close-out's gen.py, logs, check1
    # and superseded among them.
    P3_PRUNE="dry-gate gate test target"
    P3_KEEP="FACTS.md api check1 check1-answer.raw dry-logs dry-size-records dry.exit dry.out dry.sh dry.stderr gen logged.exit logged.out logged.sh logged.start logged.stderr logs out review scan scripts superseded templates"
    CLOSE_PRUNE="target"
    CLOSE_KEEP="carried check1 check1-answer.raw ci-run.log gen-change22.diff gen.diff gen.py m4p1close-ci.sh m4p1close-push.sh m4p1close-scan.sh push-pre.log push-pre.stderr push.log scan.log superseded"
    # The helpers read the directory and its two sets from PREV_DIR, PRUNE_SET
    # and KEEP_SET, set before each call of prune_dir.
    present_all() { local n; for n in $PRUNE_SET; do [ -d "$PREV_DIR/$n" ] || return 1; done; }
    gone_all() { local n; for n in $PRUNE_SET; do [ ! -e "$PREV_DIR/$n" ] || return 1; done; }
    kept_all() { local n; for n in $KEEP_SET; do [ -e "$PREV_DIR/$n" ] || return 1; done; }
    # Every name the directory holds is in exactly one of the two sets, so
    # nothing there is left unaccounted.
    accounted_all() {
      local n
      while IFS= read -r n; do
        case " $PRUNE_SET $KEEP_SET " in *" $n "*) ;; *) return 1 ;; esac
      done < <(ls -1A "$PREV_DIR")
    }
    acc_ctl() { local KEEP_SET=${KEEP_SET#* }; accounted_all; }
    kept_ctl() { local KEEP_SET="$KEEP_SET no-such-name"; kept_all; }
    gone_ctl() { local PREV_DIR=$PHASE_DIR PRUNE_SET=scripts; gone_all; }
    prune_dir() {
      local label=$1 nset nkeep prune_total=0 prune_there=0 n b
      nset=$(printf '%s\n' $PRUNE_SET | count_lines /dev/stdin)
      nkeep=$(printf '%s\n' $KEEP_SET | count_lines /dev/stdin)
      echo "  $label: <home>/${PREV_DIR#"$HOME"/}; PRUNE_PREVIOUS: $PRUNE_PREVIOUS"
      echo "  the prune set, $nset names: $PRUNE_SET"
      echo "  the kept names, $nkeep: $KEEP_SET"
      echo "command: ls -1A <home>/${PREV_DIR#"$HOME"/}, every name the directory holds before the prune"
      ls -1A "$PREV_DIR" | sed 's/^/    /'
      note "$label: every name the directory holds is in the prune set or the kept names" "$(is accounted_all)"
      note "control: accounted_all refuses the kept names one name short (the first, ${KEEP_SET%% *})" "$(isnot acc_ctl)"
      echo "command: du -sb <home>/${PREV_DIR#"$HOME"/}/<name>, for each name of the prune set"
      for n in $PRUNE_SET; do
        if [ -d "$PREV_DIR/$n" ]; then
          b=$(du -sb "$PREV_DIR/$n" | cut -f1)
          echo "    $n: $b bytes"
          prune_total=$((prune_total + b))
          prune_there=$((prune_there + 1))
        else
          echo "    $n: not there"
        fi
      done
      echo "  names of the prune set there ($label): $prune_there of $nset; their bytes in all: $prune_total"
      if [ "$PRUNE_PREVIOUS" = yes ]; then
        echo "command: rm -r <home>/${PREV_DIR#"$HOME"/}/<name>, for each name of the prune set there (no -f)"
        for n in $PRUNE_SET; do
          if [ -d "$PREV_DIR/$n" ]; then
            rm -r "${PREV_DIR:?}/${n:?}" </dev/null
            echo "    $n: rm -r exit $?"
          fi
        done
        note "$label: every name of the prune set is gone" "$(is gone_all)"
      else
        echo "  PRUNE_PREVIOUS is list: nothing removed"
        note "$label: with list, every name of the prune set is still there" "$(is present_all)"
      fi
      note "$label: every kept name is still there" "$(is kept_all)"
      note "control: kept_all refuses a list naming something not there" "$(isnot kept_ctl)"
    }
    PREV_DIR=$PREV_P3 PRUNE_SET=$P3_PRUNE KEEP_SET=$P3_KEEP
    prune_dir "M4 part 1 P3's directory"
    PREV_DIR=$PREV_CLOSE PRUNE_SET=$CLOSE_PRUNE KEEP_SET=$CLOSE_KEEP
    prune_dir "the part 1 close-out's directory"
    note "control: gone_all refuses a directory that is there (this phase's <scripts>)" "$(isnot gone_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## the spec, pinned by the hash of its committed blob (changes B33, B35 and D37; specs/0018 close-out ruling 4)"
    SPEC=specs/0031-release-metadata.md
    # The doc commit's blob's hash, read from the blob when the generator ran and
    # checked there against the 8-digit prefix planning's brief gave (change D45).
    SPEC_GAVE=18cab49d4c6906a7a2b37ecddcc88da03b372410832cdf0484f7e1247bb4c44a
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$SPEC | sha256sum; sha256sum $SPEC (the working tree's copy, printed only)"
    SPEC_SHA=$(sha256sum <"$SPEC" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    SPEC_HEAD=$(git show "$C:$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "  the phase commit's blob: sha256 $SPEC_HEAD"
    echo "  the doc commit's blob's hash, its first 8 digits the prefix planning's brief gave: $SPEC_GAVE"
    echo "  the working tree's copy, planning's (it carries planning's rulings during P1, uncommitted; change D45), not the pin: sha256 $SPEC_SHA"
    echo "command: sha256sum ROADMAP.md (the working tree's copy, planning's, printed only)"
    echo "  the working tree's ROADMAP.md: sha256 $(sha256sum <ROADMAP.md | cut -d' ' -f1)"
    note "the spec at the phase commit is the doc commit's blob" "$(is [ "$SPEC_HEAD" = "$SPEC_GAVE" ])"
    prefix_ok() { [ "${SPEC_HEAD:0:8}" = 18cab49d ]; }
    note "its first 8 digits are the prefix planning's brief gave (18cab49d)" "$(is prefix_ok)"
    prefix_ctl() { local SPEC_HEAD=$P5_SPEC_CTL; prefix_ok; }
    P5_SPEC_CTL=$(git show "$C:specs/0029-engineering-close.md" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    note "control: prefix_ok refuses specs/0029's hash at the phase commit" "$(isnot prefix_ctl)"
    S30_SPEC_CTL=$(git show "$C:specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    prefix_ctl2() { local SPEC_HEAD=$S30_SPEC_CTL; prefix_ok; }
    note "control: prefix_ok refuses specs/0030's blob at the phase commit (change D45)" "$(isnot prefix_ctl2)"
    note "control: the same comparison refuses another spec's blob (specs/0027 at the phase commit)" \
      "$(isnot [ "$(git show "$C:specs/0027-read-back.md" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" = "$SPEC_GAVE" ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits by role, read from git (header change 2)"
    note_fn() { local label=$1; shift; note "$label" "$(is "$@")"; }
    by_subject() { git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="$1" "$C"; }
    REC=$(by_subject 'M4 part 1 close-out record: the push, the CI run and the scan')
    DOC1=$(by_subject "M4 part 2 P1: commit planning docs (the part 1 close-out verification and rulings, specs/0031)")
    CHLOG=$(by_subject "M4 part 2 P1: CHANGELOG.md, the unreleased section written from the specs and records")
    DOCC=$(by_subject "M4 part 2 P1: the crate-level doc comment rewritten from the README")
    PKG=$(by_subject "M4 part 2 P1: the README and the licence texts in the package")
    echo "command: git log --format=%H -n 1 -F --grep=<the role's full subject> <phase commit>, for each role"
    echo "  part 1's close-out record commit: ${REC:-none}"
    echo "  the doc commit: ${DOC1:-none}"
    echo "  the CHANGELOG: ${CHLOG:-none}"
    echo "  the crate-level doc comment: ${DOCC:-none}"
    echo "  the README and the licence texts in the package, the phase commit: ${PKG:-none}"
    echo "command: git log -1 --format=%s <each role's commit>"
    for r in "$REC" "$DOC1" "$CHLOG" "$DOCC" "$PKG"; do
      [ -n "$r" ] && git log -1 --format='    %s' "$r"
    done
    echo "command: git rev-parse <phase commit>~0 to <phase commit>~4"
    for k in 0 1 2 3 4; do git rev-parse "$C~$k"; done | sed 's/^/    /'
    roles_in_order() {
      local r k=0
      for r in "$REC" "$DOC1" "$CHLOG" "$DOCC" "$PKG"; do
        [ -n "$r" ] || return 1
      done
      for r in "$PKG" "$DOCC" "$CHLOG" "$DOC1" "$REC"; do
        [ "$(git rev-parse "$C~$k")" = "$r" ] || return 1
        k=$((k + 1))
      done
    }
    note_fn "the doc commit, the CHANGELOG, the doc comment and the package files in that order, part 1's close-out record commit the doc commit's parent, each the next one's parent (change A45)" roles_in_order
    roles_ctl1() { local DOCC=$CHLOG; if roles_in_order; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    roles_ctl2() { local DOC1=$REC; if roles_in_order; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    roles_ctl3() { local PKG=$DOCC; if roles_in_order; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    roles_ctl4() { local CHLOG=$DOC1; if roles_in_order; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    roles_ctl5() { local DOCC=; if roles_in_order; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    note_fn "control: roles_in_order refuses the CHANGELOG commit named as the doc comment's" roles_ctl1
    note_fn "control: roles_in_order refuses the base named as the doc commit" roles_ctl2
    note_fn "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc comment commit named as the phase commit" roles_ctl3
    note_fn "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit named as the CHANGELOG's" roles_ctl4
    note_fn "control: roles_in_order refuses a role that resolved to nothing" roles_ctl5
    echo "command: git log --format=%s <part 1's close-out record commit>..<phase commit>"
    git log --format='%s' "$REC..$C" >"$W/subjects"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$W/subjects"
    PREFIX_RE='^M4 part 2 P1: '
    nsub=$(count_lines "$W/subjects")
    nprefix=$(count_matches -E "$PREFIX_RE" "$W/subjects")
    echo "  subjects in the range: $nsub; beginning \"M4 part 2 P1: \": $nprefix"
    prefix_all() { [ "$nsub" -ge 1 ] && [ "$nsub" = "$nprefix" ]; }
    note_fn "every commit in the range carries the phase's subject prefix" prefix_all
    printf 'M4 part 2 P1: x\nM4 part 2 P2: y\nM4 part 2: z\n' >"$W/c-subjects"
    ctl "one subject of three with the prefix, same command form" 1 count_matches -E "$PREFIX_RE" "$W/c-subjects"
    no_such_subject() { [ -z "$(by_subject 'M4 part 2 P1: no such subject anywhere')" ]; }
    note_fn "control: a subject no commit has resolves to nothing" no_such_subject
    echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
    echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $HEAD_SHA"
    note "the phase commit given to this script is a full sha" "$(is full_sha "$C")"
    note "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(is is_head "$C")"
    note "control: the same comparison refuses the null commit" \
      "$(is not_head "$NULL_SHA")"
    note "control: the same comparison refuses a short sha of the real commit" \
      "$(is not_head "$(printf '%s' "$C" | cut -c1-7)")"
    
    echo "phase: Milestone 4 part 2 P1 (specs/0031-release-metadata.md) gate.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "  the superseded files are kept in <home>/${PHASE_DIR#"$HOME"/}/superseded (changes A33, A35, A40, A42 to A45)"
      # specs/0014 P2 verification ruling 4: a rerun line names only hashes the
      # command under it prints.
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" \
            "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")"
        else
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time\n' \
            "$(basename "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then
        echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"
      fi
    fi
    # SERIALIZED: backed by a measurement at entry, the cargo and rustc processes
    # running before this script starts any.
    n_cargo=$(pgrep -x cargo | wc -l)
    n_rustc=$(pgrep -x rustc | wc -l)
    echo "SERIALIZED: no other log run was in flight; cargo processes at entry: $n_cargo; rustc processes at entry: $n_rustc; this run builds <repo> into <target>/main and the consumer crate into <target>/consumer (CARGO_TARGET_DIR; changes J35, K35 and K36)"
    echo "root: <repo> stands for the repository's top level, the directory this script cds to (it lies inside <home>, so it is scrubbed first); scripts/check.sh is run from it"
    echo "root: <home> stands for the home directory of the account that ran this script"
    echo "root: <phase> stands for <home>/${PHASE_DIR#"$HOME"/}, this phase's directory on the disk (change A33); <phase>/superseded keeps a superseded attempt's files; <phase>/out holds this script's own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    echo "root: <scripts> stands for <phase>/$(basename "$SELF_DIR"), the directory holding this script"
    echo "root: <build> stands for $([ -n "${GATE_BUILD_ROOT:-}" ] && echo "the directory GATE_BUILD_ROOT names, a dry run's" || echo "<phase>/gate"), this log's build directory (header change 1; change A35): the consumer crate lives in <build>/consumer, a mktemp -d directory this run makes under <build> and removes at its end (change A24), and <build>/bin/host and <build>/bin/i686 keep the copies of the DEBUG binaries, the carried form (changes J35, K38, K39 and K40)"
    echo "root: <target> stands for <phase>/target, this phase's cargo target root (specs/0029 item 2 and the specs/0001 rule it writes; changes J35, K35 and K36), one subdirectory per source tree: <target>/main for every build of <repo> (the gate, the crate's feature runs, its clippy and doc runs, the probe crate's clippy runs), as the phase's other logs and dry runs use it, and <target>/consumer for the consumer crate"
    echo "root: <scratch>/w stands for this run's mktemp -d working directory; scripts/counting.sh is read at the phase commit into <scratch>/w/counting.sh and sourced from there (change C3)"
    apart() { case "$1/" in "$2"/*) return 1 ;; esac; case "$2/" in "$1"/*) return 1 ;; esac; return 0; }
    note_fn "<scratch>/w and <phase> are distinct directories, neither inside the other" apart "$W" "$PHASE_DIR"
    note_fn "<scratch>/w and <repo> are distinct directories, neither inside the other" apart "$W" "$MAIN"
    note_fn "<phase> and <repo> are distinct directories, neither inside the other" apart "$PHASE_DIR" "$MAIN"
    note_fn "<build> and <scripts> are distinct directories, neither inside the other" apart "$BUILD_ROOT" "$SELF_DIR"
    note_fn "<build> and <target> are distinct directories, neither inside the other" apart "$BUILD_ROOT" "$SHARED_TARGET"
    note_fn "<target>/main and <target>/consumer are distinct directories, neither inside the other (change K35)" apart "$MAIN_TARGET" "$CONSUMER_TARGET"
    apart_ctl() { if apart "$BUILD_ROOT" "$PHASE_DIR"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    note_fn "control: apart refuses a directory inside another (<build> inside <phase>)" apart_ctl
    note "no cargo or rustc process was running at entry" "$(is [ "$((n_cargo + n_rustc))" = 0 ])"
    echo "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set in this shell: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    key_unset() { [ -z "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ]; }
    note "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set" "$(is key_unset)"
    key_set_ctl() { local ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=planted; key_unset; }
    note "control: the same check refuses a shell where the variable is set" "$(isnot key_set_ctl)"
    echo "DEPARTURE: CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 (this box stopped two T0 P6d gate runs for low memory)"
    echo
    echo "## script"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$SELF"
    echo
    echo "## the shared counting library this log sources"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$W/counting.sh"
    echo
    echo "## counting controls"
    counting_controls
    if [ "$counting_controls_ok" != yes ]; then fail=1; fi
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase base, resolved from git and checked for ambiguity"
    # specs/0001 requires the base to be read from git by the first doc commit's
    # subject, never typed; its parent is the base. The count of doc commits is
    # deliberately NOT asserted; structure_sound below asserts the structure.
    DOC_PATTERN='^M4 part 2 P1: commit planning docs [(]the part 1 close-out verification and rulings, specs/0031[)]'
    echo "command: git log --format='%H' --grep='$DOC_PATTERN'"
    git log --format='%H' --grep="$DOC_PATTERN" >"$W/doc-matches"
    nmatch=$(count_lines "$W/doc-matches")
    echo "  commits matching the first doc commit's pattern: $nmatch"
    note "the first doc commit's pattern matches exactly one commit" "$(is [ "$nmatch" = 1 ])"
    DOC=$(git log --format='%H' --grep="$DOC_PATTERN" -n 1)
    BASE=$(git rev-parse --verify "$DOC^" 2>/dev/null)
    echo "  the first doc commit is $DOC"
    echo "  its parent, the phase base, is $BASE"
    note "the base resolved from git, not typed" "$(is [ -n "$BASE" ])"
    CLOSE_REC=$(git log --format='%H' -n 1 --grep='^M4 part 1 close-out record:')
    echo "  part 1's close-out record commit, by subject: ${CLOSE_REC:-none found}"
    note "the phase base is part 1's close-out record commit" "$(is [ "$BASE" = "$CLOSE_REC" ])"
    note "control: the same comparison refuses the first doc commit as the base" \
      "$(isnot [ "$DOC" = "$CLOSE_REC" ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits"
    echo "command: git log --reverse --format='%H %s' <base>..<phase commit>"
    git log --reverse --format='    %H %s' "$BASE..$C"
    ncommits=$(git rev-list --count "$BASE..$C")
    echo "  commits in the range: $ncommits"
    # Each commit is classified by the paths it touches, and the sequence is
    # checked as one property in one function (change A45, P2's form again): a
    # mixed or empty commit fails, the range opens with a doc commit and holds
    # at least one code commit. CHANGELOG.md is not a planning doc, so the
    # CHANGELOG commit is a code commit.
    commit_class() {
      git show --name-only --format= "$1" | awk '
        NF { total++; if ($0 ~ /^specs\// || $0 == "ROADMAP.md" || $0 == "CLAUDE.md") docs++ }
        END {
          if (total == 0) { print "empty"; exit }
          if (docs == total) print "doc"; else if (docs == 0) print "code"; else print "mixed"
        }'
    }
    structure_sound() {
      awk 'NR == 1 && $1 != "doc" { bad = 1 }
           $1 == "mixed" || $1 == "empty" { bad = 1 }
           $1 == "code" { code = 1 }
           END { exit (bad || !code || NR == 0) }' "$1"
    }
    : >"$W/classes"
    for h in $(git rev-list --reverse "$BASE..$C"); do
      printf '%s %s\n' "$(commit_class "$h")" "$(git log --format='%h %s' -n 1 "$h")" >>"$W/classes"
    done
    sed 's/^/    /' "$W/classes"
    note "every commit is planning docs alone or code alone, the range opens with a doc commit and holds code (change A45)" \
      "$(is structure_sound "$W/classes")"
    ndoc=$(count_matches -E '^doc ' "$W/classes")
    ncode=$(count_matches -E '^code ' "$W/classes")
    echo "  of the $ncommits commits in the range: $ndoc planning-doc, $ncode code"
    note "the phase holds at least one doc commit, counted in the range" \
      "$(is [ "$ndoc" -ge 1 ])"
    note "control: the same count finds this phase's code commits too" \
      "$(is [ "$ncode" -ge 1 ])"
    note "control: the two classes account for every commit in the range" \
      "$(is [ "$((ndoc + ncode))" = "$ncommits" ])"
    note "control: commit_class calls the first doc commit a doc commit" \
      "$(is [ "$(commit_class "$DOC")" = doc ])"
    # The code-commit control names its commit by what that commit DID: the
    # commit in the range that modified crates/emend/src/lib.rs (change A45).
    CODEC=$(git log --format='%H' -n 1 --diff-filter=M "$BASE..$C" -- crates/emend/src/lib.rs)
    echo "  the commit in the range that modified crates/emend/src/lib.rs: ${CODEC:-none found}"
    note "the commit that modified crates/emend/src/lib.rs resolved from git" "$(is [ -n "$CODEC" ])"
    note "control: commit_class calls the commit that modified crates/emend/src/lib.rs a code commit" \
      "$(is [ "$(commit_class "$CODEC")" = code ])"
    note "control: commit_class calls part 1's close-out record commit, logs alone, a code commit (not a doc commit)" \
      "$(is [ "$(commit_class "$CLOSE_REC")" = code ])"
    note "control: the first doc commit carries specs/0031, a path the classifier reads as a doc" \
      "$(is [ "$(git show --name-only --format= "$DOC" | count_matches -Fx specs/0031-release-metadata.md /dev/stdin)" = 1 ])"
    printf 'doc a docs\ncode b code\ndoc c docs\ncode d code\n' >"$W/c-ord-ok"
    printf 'code a code\ndoc b docs\n'                        >"$W/c-ord-first"
    printf 'doc a docs\nmixed b both\ncode c code\n'          >"$W/c-ord-mixed"
    printf 'doc a docs\nempty b nothing\ncode c code\n'       >"$W/c-ord-empty"
    printf 'doc a docs\ndoc b docs\n'                         >"$W/c-ord-nocode"
    note "control: structure_sound accepts docs and code interleaved" \
      "$(is structure_sound "$W/c-ord-ok")"
    note "control: structure_sound rejects a range that opens with a code commit" \
      "$(isnot structure_sound "$W/c-ord-first")"
    note "control: structure_sound rejects a commit mixing docs and code" \
      "$(isnot structure_sound "$W/c-ord-mixed")"
    note "control: structure_sound rejects an empty commit" \
      "$(isnot structure_sound "$W/c-ord-empty")"
    note "control: isnot reports a passing command as UNEXPECTED, so it can fail" \
      "$(is [ "$(isnot true)" = UNEXPECTED ])"
    note "control: structure_sound rejects a range with no code commit" \
      "$(isnot structure_sound "$W/c-ord-nocode")"
    # Change A37, kept (A38): every doc commit before every code commit.
    docs_first() { awk '$1 == "code" { c = 1 } $1 == "doc" && c { bad = 1 } END { exit bad }' "$1"; }
    note "no doc commit follows a code commit in the range (changes A37 to A40, A42 to A45)" "$(is docs_first "$W/classes")"
    printf 'doc a docs\ndoc b docs\ncode c code\ncode d code\n' >"$W/c-ord-first-docs"
    note "control: docs_first accepts two doc commits before two code commits" "$(is docs_first "$W/c-ord-first-docs")"
    note "control: docs_first refuses docs and code interleaved" "$(isnot docs_first "$W/c-ord-ok")"
    
    echo
    echo "## every commit message in the range: ASCII, ending with the Co-Authored-By line only"
    COAUTHOR='Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>'
    msg_form_ok() {
      local last nco nsess nna ntrail
      last=$(awk 'NF { l = $0 } END { print l }' "$1")
      nco=$(count_matches -E '^Co-Authored-By:' "$1")
      nsess=$(count_matches_i -F 'claude-session' "$1")
      nna=$(count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$1")
      ntrail=$(git interpret-trailers --parse <"$1" | count_lines /dev/stdin)
      [ "$last" = "$COAUTHOR" ] || return 1
      [ "$nco" = 1 ] || return 1
      [ "$nsess" = 0 ] || return 1
      [ "$ntrail" = 1 ] || return 1
      [ "$nna" = 0 ]
    }
    for h in $(git rev-list --reverse "$BASE..$C"); do
      git log -1 --format=%B "$h" >"$W/msg"
      echo "  $(git log -1 --format=%h "$h"): message lines $(count_lines "$W/msg"), non-ASCII bytes $(count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$W/msg"), trailers git parses:"
      git interpret-trailers --parse <"$W/msg" | sed 's/^/      /'
      note "$(git log -1 --format=%h "$h")'s message is ASCII and ends with the Co-Authored-By line only" \
        "$(is msg_form_ok "$W/msg")"
    done
    printf 'subject\n\nbody\n\n%s\n' "$COAUTHOR" >"$W/c-msg-ok"
    printf 'subject\n\nbody\n\n%s\n%s: x\n' "$COAUTHOR" 'Claude-Session' >"$W/c-msg-session"
    printf 'subj\303\251ct\n\n%s\n' "$COAUTHOR" >"$W/c-msg-nonascii"
    printf 'subject\n\n%s\n%s\n' "$COAUTHOR" "$COAUTHOR" >"$W/c-msg-twice"
    printf 'subject\n\nbody\n' >"$W/c-msg-none"
    note "control: msg_form_ok accepts a message ending with the line" "$(is msg_form_ok "$W/c-msg-ok")"
    note "control: msg_form_ok refuses a session line after it" "$(isnot msg_form_ok "$W/c-msg-session")"
    note "control: msg_form_ok refuses a non-ASCII byte" "$(isnot msg_form_ok "$W/c-msg-nonascii")"
    note "control: msg_form_ok refuses the line twice" "$(isnot msg_form_ok "$W/c-msg-twice")"
    note "control: msg_form_ok refuses a message without it" "$(isnot msg_form_ok "$W/c-msg-none")"
    # Change J3 (specs/0018 P2 verification ruling 5 and P3 verification ruling
    # 2, G9, carried in the scan script's form): the count rule on EVERY commit
    # of the phase. A message passes when it carries the diff-alone sentence,
    # read with its line breaks folded, or when it states no count. counts_in
    # prints the numbers left in the body (the trailer dropped) once identifiers
    # are removed: words holding a slash (paths), tokens such as P1 or M2, and the
    # number after "ruling", "decision", "part", "phase" or "section", with any
    # "to" or "and" range after it; what is left, a whole-word number in digits or
    # a number word to twenty, is a count.
    COUNT_SENTENCE='No log prints a count for this commit; the diff alone carries what it changes.'
    says_diff_alone() { tr '\n' ' ' <"$1" | tr -s ' ' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qF "$COUNT_SENTENCE"; }
    counts_in() {
      python3 - "$1" <<'COUNTS'
    import re, sys
    text = open(sys.argv[1]).read()
    body = "\n".join(l for l in text.split("\n") if not re.match(r"^Co-Authored-By:", l))
    body = " ".join(body.split())
    body = " ".join(w for w in body.split(" ") if "/" not in w)
    body = re.sub(r"\b[A-Z][0-9]+\b", " ", body)
    num = r"(?:[0-9]+|one|two|three|four|five|six|seven|eight|nine|ten|eleven|twelve|thirteen|fourteen|fifteen|sixteen|seventeen|eighteen|nineteen|twenty)"
    body = re.sub(r"\b(?:rulings?|decisions?|parts?|phases?|sections?)\b[^.;:]*?\b" + num + r"\b(?:,? (?:to|and) " + num + r"\b)*", " ", body, flags=re.I)
    for m in re.finditer(r"\b" + num + r"\b", body, flags=re.I):
        print(m.group(0))
    COUNTS
    }
    states_no_count() { [ -z "$(counts_in "$1")" ]; }
    count_rule_ok() { says_diff_alone "$1" || states_no_count "$1"; }
    for h in $(git rev-list --reverse "$BASE..$C"); do
      git log -1 --format=%B "$h" >"$W/msg-rule"
      found=$(counts_in "$W/msg-rule" | tr '\n' ' ')
      sentence=$(says_diff_alone "$W/msg-rule" && echo yes || echo no)
      echo "  $(git log -1 --format=%h "$h"): counts left after the identifiers: ${found:-none}; the diff-alone sentence: $sentence"
      note "$(git log -1 --format=%h "$h")'s message states no count or says the diff alone carries its counts (change J3)" "$(is count_rule_ok "$W/msg-rule")"
    done
    printf 'subject\n\nNo log prints a count for this\ncommit; the diff alone carries what it changes.\n' >"$W/c-msg-folded"
    note "control: says_diff_alone reads the sentence across a line break" "$(is says_diff_alone "$W/c-msg-folded")"
    note "control: says_diff_alone refuses a message without it" "$(isnot says_diff_alone "$W/c-msg-ok")"
    printf 'M4 part 2 P1: x\n\nThe rulings during P1, 1 to 3, and decisions 4 to 6 A; specs/0027-x.md.\n\n%s\n' "$COAUTHOR" >"$W/c-rule-ids"
    printf 'M4 part 2 P1: x\n\nAdds three tests and 14 lines.\n\n%s\n' "$COAUTHOR" >"$W/c-rule-count"
    printf 'M4 part 2 P1: x\n\nAdds three tests. No log prints a count for this commit; the\ndiff alone carries what it changes.\n\n%s\n' "$COAUTHOR" >"$W/c-rule-both"
    note "control: count_rule_ok accepts a message whose numbers are identifiers and a trailer" "$(is count_rule_ok "$W/c-rule-ids")"
    note "control: count_rule_ok refuses a message stating counts without the sentence" "$(isnot count_rule_ok "$W/c-rule-count")"
    note "control: count_rule_ok accepts the same counts beside the sentence" "$(is count_rule_ok "$W/c-rule-both")"
    ctl "counts_in finds the two counts of the refused message, same command form" 2 run_lines counts_in "$W/c-rule-count"
    
    echo
    echo "## the doc commit's files against the hashes of its blobs and against the hashes its own message gives; the lines it removes printed (header change 3; changes B33, B35, D38 to D42, D43, D44 and D45)"
    # The expected values were read from the doc commit's blobs when the
    # generator ran, each checked there against the 8-digit prefix planning's
    # brief gave (change D45). Every computed hash is printed by the command
    # that made it.
    echo "  the doc commit: $DOC1"
    blob_sha() { git show "$1:$2" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1; }
    blob_matches() {
      git cat-file -e "$1:$2" 2>/dev/null || return 1
      [ "$(blob_sha "$1" "$2")" = "$3" ]
    }
    while read -r which path given prefix; do
      case "$which" in doc1) at=$DOC1 ;; head) at=$C ;; esac
      if git cat-file -e "$at:$path" 2>/dev/null; then got=$(blob_sha "$at" "$path"); else got=absent; fi
      echo "  $which $(git rev-parse --short "$at") $path"
      echo "    command: git show <commit>:$path | sha256sum"
      echo "    sha256 $got"
      echo "    the doc commit's blob's hash: $given (the prefix planning's brief gave: $prefix)"
      note "$which's $path is the doc commit's blob" "$(is blob_matches "$at" "$path" "$given")"
      note "the hash this check expects begins with the brief's prefix" "$(is [ "${given:0:8}" = "$prefix" ])"
    done <<'HASHES'
    doc1 specs/0031-release-metadata.md 18cab49d4c6906a7a2b37ecddcc88da03b372410832cdf0484f7e1247bb4c44a 18cab49d
    doc1 specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md 07886b16373a0a5effe8d45091304ad0278a23364276a9711615131872fdf137 07886b16
    doc1 ROADMAP.md 9f1fd354e01822b380e909f175866924fd58eaba4bd87874920b15ccc1ad42ce 9f1fd354
    head specs/0031-release-metadata.md 18cab49d4c6906a7a2b37ecddcc88da03b372410832cdf0484f7e1247bb4c44a 18cab49d
    head specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md 07886b16373a0a5effe8d45091304ad0278a23364276a9711615131872fdf137 07886b16
    head ROADMAP.md 9f1fd354e01822b380e909f175866924fd58eaba4bd87874920b15ccc1ad42ce 9f1fd354
    HASHES
    TAB=$(printf '\t')
    git show --name-status --format= "$DOC1" | LC_ALL=C sort -k2 >"$W/doc1-files"
    printf '%s\n' "M${TAB}ROADMAP.md" "M${TAB}specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md" "A${TAB}specs/0031-release-metadata.md" | LC_ALL=C sort -k2 >"$W/doc1-want"
    sed 's/^/    the doc commit carries: /' "$W/doc1-files"
    note "the doc commit adds specs/0031 and modifies specs/0030 and ROADMAP.md, nothing else (change D45)" "$(is cmp -s "$W/doc1-files" "$W/doc1-want")"
    printf '%s\n' "M${TAB}ROADMAP.md" "M${TAB}specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md" "M${TAB}specs/0031-release-metadata.md" | LC_ALL=C sort -k2 >"$W/c-doc1-status"
    note "control: the comparison refuses specs/0031 modified rather than added" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/c-doc1-status" "$W/doc1-want")"
    note "control: blob_matches refuses the doc commit's specs/0031 hash at the base, which lacks the file (change D45)" \
      "$(isnot blob_matches "$BASE" specs/0031-release-metadata.md 18cab49d4c6906a7a2b37ecddcc88da03b372410832cdf0484f7e1247bb4c44a)"
    note "control: blob_matches refuses the doc commit's specs/0030 hash at the base, which holds part 1's copy (change D45)" \
      "$(isnot blob_matches "$BASE" specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md 07886b16373a0a5effe8d45091304ad0278a23364276a9711615131872fdf137)"
    note "control: blob_matches refuses the doc commit's ROADMAP.md hash at the base, which holds part 1's copy (change D45)" \
      "$(isnot blob_matches "$BASE" ROADMAP.md 9f1fd354e01822b380e909f175866924fd58eaba4bd87874920b15ccc1ad42ce)"
    # The doc commit's own message gives each file's hash as "<path> sha256
    # <hash>", a line break allowed anywhere between the three; its lines are
    # folded and the pairs read, then compared as a set with the three blobs'
    # pairs built the same way.
    git log -1 --format=%B "$DOC1" >"$W/doc1-msg"
    msg_hash_pairs() {
      tr '\n' ' ' <"$1" | tr -s ' ' |
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E '[^ ()]+ sha256 [0-9a-f]{64}' | LC_ALL=C sort -u || :
    }
    msg_hash_pairs "$W/doc1-msg" >"$W/doc1-msg-hashes"
    for path in specs/0031-release-metadata.md specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md ROADMAP.md; do
      printf '%s sha256 %s\n' "$path" "$(blob_sha "$DOC1" "$path")"
    done | LC_ALL=C sort -u >"$W/doc1-blob-hashes"
    echo "command: git log -1 --format=%B <doc commit>, line breaks folded, each '<path> sha256 <hash>' read; and, for the three files, the path, sha256 and git show <doc commit>:<path> | sha256sum"
    sed 's/^/    the doc commit'"'"'s message holds: /' "$W/doc1-msg-hashes"
    sed 's/^/    the doc commit'"'"'s blobs hash: /' "$W/doc1-blob-hashes"
    note "the doc commit's message gives exactly its three blobs' hashes, in full (change D45)" "$(is cmp -s "$W/doc1-msg-hashes" "$W/doc1-blob-hashes")"
    sed '$ s/.$/0/' "$W/doc1-blob-hashes" >"$W/c-doc1-lines"
    if cmp -s "$W/c-doc1-lines" "$W/doc1-blob-hashes"; then sed '$ s/.$/1/' "$W/doc1-blob-hashes" >"$W/c-doc1-lines"; fi
    sed -E 's/^([^ ]+) sha256 ([0-9a-f]{64})$/\1\nsha256 \2 and/' "$W/c-doc1-lines" >"$W/c-doc1-msg"
    msg_hash_pairs "$W/c-doc1-msg" >"$W/c-doc1-msg-hashes"
    note "control: the same check refuses a message whose last hash differs in its last digit" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/c-doc1-msg-hashes" "$W/doc1-blob-hashes")"
    ctl "the pairs in a planted message of three, each broken across a line, same command form" 3 run_lines msg_hash_pairs "$W/c-doc1-msg"
    sed '$d' "$W/doc1-want" >"$W/c-doc-short"
    note "control: the file comparison refuses a list one file short" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/c-doc-short" "$W/doc1-want")"
    # Change D45: the lines the doc commit removes are planning's text and are
    # printed (specs/0031 is added, so it removes none).
    removed_count() { LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^-' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vcE '^--- ' || :; }
    for path in specs/0031-release-metadata.md specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md ROADMAP.md; do
      git show -U0 --format= "$DOC1" -- "$path" >"$W/doc1-diff"
      echo "command: git show -U0 --format= <doc commit> -- $path, the lines removed (a leading -, not the --- file line)"
      echo "  $path: lines removed $(removed_count "$W/doc1-diff")"
      git show -U0 --format= "$DOC1" -- "$path" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^-' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vE '^--- ' | sed 's#^#    '"$path"' removes (planning'"'"'s): #' || :
    done
    printf -- '--- a/x\n+++ b/x\n@@ -1,2 +1,1 @@\n-gone line\n' >"$W/c-removed"
    ctl "removed lines in a planted diff of one removal, same command form" 1 removed_count "$W/c-removed"
    
    echo
    echo "## each commit's diff and the phase's combined diff, hashed with the command that produced each"
    for h in $(git rev-list --reverse "$BASE..$C"); do
      cmd="git show --no-color --no-ext-diff --format= $h"
      echo "  command: $cmd | sha256sum"
      echo "    $($cmd | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)  $(git log -1 --format=%s "$h")"
    done
    cmd="git diff --no-color --no-ext-diff $BASE $C"
    echo "  command: $cmd | sha256sum"
    echo "    $($cmd | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)  the phase's combined diff"
    h1=$(git show --no-color --no-ext-diff --format= "$C" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    h2=$(git show --no-color --no-ext-diff --format= "$C" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    h3=$(git show --no-color --no-ext-diff --format= "$C^" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    note "control: the phase commit's diff hashes the same twice" "$(is [ "$h1" = "$h2" ])"
    note "control: its parent's diff hashes differently" "$(isnot [ "$h1" = "$h3" ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the changed files at the phase commit"
    for f in $(git diff --name-only --diff-filter=d "$BASE" "$C"); do
      git show "$C:$f" >"$W/f" 2>/dev/null || { echo "$f: READ ERROR"; fail=1; continue; }
      echo "$f: sha256 $(sha256sum <"$W/f" | cut -d' ' -f1), bytes $(wc -c <"$W/f"), mode $(git ls-tree "$C" -- "$f" | awk '{print $1}')"
    done
    git diff --name-only --diff-filter=d "$BASE" "$C" >"$W/difffiles"
    echo "  files in the diff: $(count_lines "$W/difffiles")"
    new_mode() { [ "$(git ls-tree "$C" -- "$1" | awk '{print $1}')" = 100755 ]; }
    # Change G37, kept (G38): a modified file keeps its base mode, and an added
    # file is not executable.
    mode_at() { git ls-tree "$1" -- "$2" | awk '{print $1}'; }
    mode_kept() { [ -n "$(mode_at "$BASE" "$1")" ] && [ "$(mode_at "$BASE" "$1")" = "$(mode_at "$C" "$1")" ]; }
    git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A "$BASE" "$C" >"$W/mode-added"
    git diff --name-only --diff-filter=M "$BASE" "$C" >"$W/mode-modified"
    while IFS= read -r m; do
      echo "  $m (modified): mode at the base $(mode_at "$BASE" "$m"); at the phase commit $(mode_at "$C" "$m")"
      note "$m keeps its base mode (change G37)" "$(is mode_kept "$m")"
    done <"$W/mode-modified"
    while IFS= read -r m; do
      echo "  $m (added): mode at the phase commit $(mode_at "$C" "$m")"
      note "$m, added in this phase, is not executable" "$(isnot new_mode "$m")"
    done <"$W/mode-added"
    note "control: the same mode check finds the runner executable" "$(is new_mode scripts/passthrough-run.sh)"
    note "control: the same mode check refuses the spec (M3 part 1 P2's change C19, carried)" "$(isnot new_mode specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md)"
    mode_kept_ctl() { mode_kept no/such/path/in/either/commit; }
    note "control: mode_kept refuses a path neither commit holds (changes G38 to G40, G42 to G45)" "$(isnot mode_kept_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## the gate files this phase changed, and the self-test they require"
    # specs/0001-bootstrap.md, "Rules for every phase": a phase that changes no
    # gate file LISTS IN gate.log the gate files it checked against the diff.
    cat >"$W/gate-files" <<'EOF'
    scripts/check.sh
    scripts/privacy.sh
    scripts/privacy-patterns.txt
    scripts/privacy-identity.txt
    scripts/sys-allowlist.txt
    scripts/install-hooks.sh
    scripts/counting.sh
    scripts/gate-self-test.sh
    .gitignore
    .github/workflows/ci.yml
    EOF
    echo "command: awk over specs/0001-bootstrap.md, the bullet opening '- A phase that changes a gate file' up to its first 'runs', backticked names"
    git show "$C:specs/0001-bootstrap.md" | awk '/^- A phase that changes a gate file/ { on = 1 } on { print } on && /runs/ { exit }' >"$W/gate-sentence"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$W/gate-sentence"
    tr -d '\n' <"$W/gate-sentence" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E '`[^`]+`' | tr -d '`' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -v -E ' ' | sort >"$W/gate-from-spec"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -v -Fx .github/workflows/ci.yml "$W/gate-files" | sort >"$W/gate-typed"
    sed 's/^/    named in specs\/0001: /' "$W/gate-from-spec"
    ci_named() { [ "$(count_matches -F 'the CI workflow' "$W/gate-sentence")" = 1 ]; }
    note "the typed gate-file list is specs/0001's backticked names plus the CI workflow" "$(is cmp -s "$W/gate-from-spec" "$W/gate-typed")"
    note "specs/0001's sentence names the CI workflow" "$(is ci_named)"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -v -Fx scripts/counting.sh "$W/gate-typed" >"$W/c-gate-typed"
    note "control: the comparison refuses the typed list one name short" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/gate-from-spec" "$W/c-gate-typed")"
    echo "  the gate files specs/0001 names, each checked against the phase diff:"
    sed 's/^/    checked: /' "$W/gate-files"
    touched=0
    while IFS= read -r g; do
      if LC_ALL=C "$G" -Fxq -- "$g" "$W/difffiles"; then
        echo "  gate file in the diff: $g"
        touched=$((touched + 1))
      fi
    done <"$W/gate-files"
    echo "  gate files checked: $(count_lines "$W/gate-files"); of them in the phase diff: $touched"
    note "no gate file is in the phase diff, so specs/0001 asks for this listing and no self-test (changes F38 and F40)" \
      "$(is [ "$touched" = 0 ])"
    FIRST_DIFF=$(sed -n '1p' "$W/difffiles")
    echo "  a file that IS in the phase diff, taken from the diff: $FIRST_DIFF"
    found_first=$(count_matches -Fx "$FIRST_DIFF" "$W/difffiles")
    note "control: the same search finds a name the diff does hold" \
      "$(is [ "$found_first" -ge 1 ])"
    in_diff_not_gate() {
      [ "$(count_matches -Fx "$1" "$W/difffiles")" = 1 ] &&
        [ "$(count_matches -Fx "$1" "$W/gate-files")" = 0 ]
    }
    # Every file the phase diff holds, read from the diff rather than typed.
    while IFS= read -r s; do
      echo "  $s: in the phase diff $(count_matches -Fx "$s" "$W/difffiles") times; in the gate-file list $(count_matches -Fx "$s" "$W/gate-files") times"
      note "$s is in the diff and is not a gate file" "$(is in_diff_not_gate "$s")"
    done <"$W/difffiles"
    gate_ctl() { in_diff_not_gate scripts/counting.sh; }
    note "control: in_diff_not_gate refuses a gate file the phase diff does not hold (scripts/counting.sh)" "$(isnot gate_ctl)"
    ST=records/logs/m4p2-p1/self-test.log
    echo "  $ST: $([ -e "$ST" ] && echo PRESENT || echo "absent, as a phase with no gate-file change requires")"
    note "this phase committed no self-test log, having changed no gate file (changes F38, F40 to F44 and F45)" \
      "$(is [ ! -e "$ST" ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## each code commit touches its own files only, each with the status git gives it; the tree at the phase commit the base's outside the phase's files; the doc comment doc lines alone; the manifest gaining the readme line alone; the licence copies the root's blobs; no other Rust source, no lock, tool or script in the range; README.md not in the range (change E45)"
    TAB=$(printf '\t')
    printf '%s\n' "A${TAB}CHANGELOG.md" >"$W/area-want-CHLOG"
    printf '%s\n' "M${TAB}crates/emend/src/lib.rs" >"$W/area-want-DOCC"
    printf '%s\n' "M${TAB}crates/emend/Cargo.toml" "A${TAB}crates/emend/LICENSE-APACHE" "A${TAB}crates/emend/LICENSE-MIT" | LC_ALL=C sort -k2 >"$W/area-want-PKG"
    for role in CHLOG DOCC PKG; do
      at=${!role}
      echo "command: git show --name-status --format= <$role> | sort -k2"
      git show --name-status --format= "$at" | LC_ALL=C sort -k2 >"$W/area-$role"
      sed 's/^/    /' "$W/area-$role"
      note "$role's files are the ones FACTS.md gives, with the status git gives each (change E45)" "$(is cmp -s "$W/area-$role" "$W/area-want-$role")"
    done
    note "control: the comparison refuses the CHANGELOG commit's files given as the doc comment's" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/area-CHLOG" "$W/area-want-DOCC")"
    printf '%s\n' "M${TAB}CHANGELOG.md" >"$W/c-area"
    note "control: the comparison refuses CHANGELOG.md modified rather than added" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/c-area" "$W/area-want-CHLOG")"
    # same_outside <a> <b> <path>...: git diff --quiet between the two commits
    # over every path but the ones given.
    PHASE_FILES="specs/0031-release-metadata.md specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md ROADMAP.md CHANGELOG.md crates/emend/src/lib.rs crates/emend/Cargo.toml crates/emend/LICENSE-MIT crates/emend/LICENSE-APACHE"
    same_outside() {
      local a=$1 b=$2 p
      shift 2
      local spec=(.)
      for p in "$@"; do spec+=(":!$p"); done
      git diff --quiet "$a" "$b" -- "${spec[@]}"
    }
    echo "command: git diff --stat <base> <phase commit> -- . ':!<each of the phase's files>'"
    echo "  the phase's files: $PHASE_FILES"
    same_spec=(.)
    for p in $PHASE_FILES; do same_spec+=(":!$p"); done
    git diff --stat "$BASE" "$C" -- "${same_spec[@]}" | sed 's/^/    /'
    note "the tree at the phase commit is the base's outside the phase's files (change E45)" "$(is same_outside "$BASE" "$C" $PHASE_FILES)"
    same_ctl() { same_outside "$BASE" "$C" $(printf '%s\n' $PHASE_FILES | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vFx crates/emend/src/lib.rs); }
    note "control: the same check refuses the exclusions with lib.rs left out" "$(isnot same_ctl)"
    # doc_lines_only <diff file>: every added or removed line, the file lines
    # (+++ and ---) aside, starts //! after its sign, and there is at least one.
    doc_lines_only() {
      local n_all n_doc
      n_all=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^[-+]' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vE '^(\+\+\+|---) ' | count_lines /dev/stdin)
      n_doc=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^[-+]//!' "$1" | count_lines /dev/stdin)
      [ "$n_all" -ge 1 ] && [ "$n_all" = "$n_doc" ]
    }
    git diff --no-color -U0 "$DOCC^" "$DOCC" -- crates/emend/src/lib.rs >"$W/docc-diff"
    git diff --no-color -U0 "$BASE" "$C" -- crates/emend/src >"$W/src-diff"
    echo "command: git diff -U0 <doc comment commit>^ <doc comment commit> -- crates/emend/src/lib.rs; git diff -U0 <base> <phase commit> -- crates/emend/src"
    echo "  the doc comment commit: lines added $(LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^\+' "$W/docc-diff" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vE '^\+\+\+ ' | count_lines /dev/stdin), removed $(LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^-' "$W/docc-diff" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vE '^--- ' | count_lines /dev/stdin); of them starting //! after the sign: $(LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^[-+]//!' "$W/docc-diff" | count_lines /dev/stdin)"
    echo "  the range's diff of crates/emend/src: files $(LC_ALL=C "$G" -cE '^diff --git ' "$W/src-diff")"
    note "the doc comment commit's diff holds doc lines alone (decision 3; change E45)" "$(is doc_lines_only "$W/docc-diff")"
    note "the range's diff of crates/emend/src holds doc lines alone (change E45)" "$(is doc_lines_only "$W/src-diff")"
    cp "$W/docc-diff" "$W/c-docc-diff"
    printf '+pub fn planted() {}\n' >>"$W/c-docc-diff"
    note "control: doc_lines_only refuses the same diff with a planted code line" "$(isnot doc_lines_only "$W/c-docc-diff")"
    : >"$W/c-empty-diff"
    note "control: doc_lines_only refuses an empty diff" "$(isnot doc_lines_only "$W/c-empty-diff")"
    # The manifest: over the range, exactly one line added, the readme line,
    # none removed, and at the phase commit the line before it is publish =
    # false (decision 4; P1 ruling 3).
    MAN=crates/emend/Cargo.toml
    README_LINE='readme = "../../README.md"'
    man_added() { git diff --no-color -U0 "$1" "$2" -- "$MAN" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^\+' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vE '^\+\+\+ ' | sed 's/^+//' || :; }
    man_removed() { git diff --no-color -U0 "$1" "$2" -- "$MAN" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^-' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vE '^--- ' | count_lines /dev/stdin; }
    before_readme() { git show "$1:$MAN" | awk -v l="$README_LINE" '$0 == l { print p; exit } { p = $0 }'; }
    echo "command: git diff -U0 <base> <phase commit> -- $MAN, the lines added and the count removed; git show <commit>:$MAN | awk, the line before the readme line"
    man_added "$BASE" "$C" | sed 's/^/    added: /'
    echo "  lines removed: $(man_removed "$BASE" "$C"); the line before the readme line at the phase commit: $(before_readme "$C")"
    man_ok() {
      [ "$(man_added "$1" "$2")" = "$README_LINE" ] && [ "$(man_removed "$1" "$2")" = 0 ] &&
        [ "$(before_readme "$2")" = "publish = false" ]
    }
    note "the manifest gains the readme line alone, directly after publish = false, over the range (P1 ruling 3; change E45)" "$(is man_ok "$BASE" "$C")"
    man_ctl() { man_ok "$BASE" "$BASE"; }
    note "control: man_ok refuses the base against itself, where the line is not there" "$(isnot man_ctl)"
    # The licence copies: each copy's blob is the root file's blob at the phase
    # commit (decision 4).
    blob_id() { git rev-parse "$1:$2" 2>/dev/null; }
    same_blob() { [ -n "$(blob_id "$C" "$1")" ] && [ "$(blob_id "$C" "$1")" = "$(blob_id "$C" "$2")" ]; }
    echo "command: git rev-parse <phase commit>:<path>, for each licence copy and its root file"
    for pair in "crates/emend/LICENSE-MIT LICENSE-MIT" "crates/emend/LICENSE-APACHE LICENSE-APACHE"; do
      read -r lcopy lroot <<<"$pair"
      echo "  $lcopy: blob $(blob_id "$C" "$lcopy"); $lroot: blob $(blob_id "$C" "$lroot")"
      note "$lcopy is $lroot's blob at the phase commit (decision 4; change E45)" "$(is same_blob "$lcopy" "$lroot")"
    done
    lic_ctl() { same_blob crates/emend/LICENSE-MIT LICENSE-APACHE; }
    note "control: same_blob refuses the MIT copy paired with the Apache text" "$(isnot lic_ctl)"
    # No other Rust source, no lock, nothing under tools/ or scripts/.
    range_paths() { git diff --name-only "$1" "$2" -- '*.rs' Cargo.lock 'tools/*' 'scripts/*' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vFx crates/emend/src/lib.rs | count_lines /dev/stdin; }
    nrange=$(range_paths "$BASE" "$C")
    echo "command: git diff --name-only <base> <phase commit> -- '*.rs' Cargo.lock 'tools/*' 'scripts/*', crates/emend/src/lib.rs aside"
    git diff --name-only "$BASE" "$C" -- '*.rs' Cargo.lock 'tools/*' 'scripts/*' | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  Rust sources but lib.rs, the lock, tools and scripts changed in the range: $nrange"
    note "the range changes no Rust source but lib.rs, no Cargo.lock and nothing under tools/ or scripts/ (change E45)" "$(is [ "$nrange" = 0 ])"
    ARCHC=$(git log --format='%H' -n 1 --diff-filter=M -- crates/emend/src/archive.rs)
    echo "  the last commit that modified crates/emend/src/archive.rs: ${ARCHC:-none found}"
    rs_ctl() { [ -n "$ARCHC" ] && [ "$(range_paths "$ARCHC^" "$ARCHC")" -ge 1 ]; }
    note "control: the same count finds the last commit that modified archive.rs" "$(is rs_ctl)"
    LOCKC=$(git log --format='%H' -n 1 -- Cargo.lock)
    echo "  the last commit that changed Cargo.lock: ${LOCKC:-none found}"
    lockc_touched() { [ -n "$LOCKC" ] && [ "$(range_paths "$LOCKC^" "$LOCKC")" -ge 1 ]; }
    note "control: the same count finds the last commit that changed Cargo.lock" "$(is lockc_touched)"
    SCRC=$(git log --format='%H' -n 1 -- 'scripts/*')
    echo "  the last commit that changed a file under scripts/: ${SCRC:-none found}"
    scrc_touched() { [ -n "$SCRC" ] && [ "$(range_paths "$SCRC^" "$SCRC")" -ge 1 ]; }
    note "control: the same count finds the last commit that changed a script" "$(is scrc_touched)"
    # README.md is not in the range (P1's form, change E42).
    readme_in_range() { [ "$(git diff --name-only "$1" "$2" -- README.md | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; }
    echo "command: git diff --name-only <base> <phase commit> -- README.md"
    git diff --name-only "$BASE" "$C" -- README.md | sed 's/^/    /'
    note "README.md is not in the range's diff (change E45)" "$(is readme_in_range "$BASE" "$C")"
    README_C=$(git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="M3 part 7 P5: the README's two sentences")
    echo "  M3 part 7 P5's README commit, by subject: ${README_C:-none found}"
    readme_ctl() { [ -n "$README_C" ] && readme_in_range "$README_C^" "$README_C"; }
    note "control: the same check refuses M3 part 7 P5's README commit, which changed it" "$(isnot readme_ctl)"
    # The crate's messages: every Error::Package("...") string under
    # crates/emend/src, as a set, the same at the base and the phase commit.
    messages_set() { git grep -h -o -E 'Error::Package[(]"[^"]*"[)]' "$1" -- crates/emend/src | LC_ALL=C sort -u; }
    messages_set "$BASE" >"$W/msgs-base"
    messages_set "$C" >"$W/msgs-head"
    echo "command: git grep -h -o -E 'Error::Package[(]\"[^\"]*\"[)]' <commit> -- crates/emend/src | sort -u, at the base and at the phase commit"
    echo "  distinct messages at the base: $(count_lines "$W/msgs-base"); at the phase commit: $(count_lines "$W/msgs-head")"
    note "the crate's Error::Package messages are the base's, as a set (change E40)" "$(is cmp -s "$W/msgs-base" "$W/msgs-head")"
    note "some messages were read" "$(is [ "$(count_lines "$W/msgs-head")" -ge 1 ])"
    sed '1d' "$W/msgs-head" >"$W/c-msgs"
    note "control: the comparison refuses the set one message short" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/msgs-base" "$W/c-msgs")"
    
    echo
    echo "## every script under scripts/ parses or compiles at the phase commit (changes H37 to H40, H42 to H45)"
    parse_ok() { bash -n "$1" 2>/dev/null; }
    echo "command: git ls-tree --name-only <phase commit> scripts/, each .sh through bash -n and each .py through py_compile (doraise)"
    git ls-tree --name-only "$C" scripts/ >"$W/scripts-all"
    nsh=0; npyall=0
    while IFS= read -r s; do
      case "$s" in
        *.sh)
          git show "$C:$s" >"$W/parse.sh"
          note "$s parses at the phase commit" "$(is parse_ok "$W/parse.sh")"
          nsh=$((nsh + 1)) ;;
      esac
    done <"$W/scripts-all"
    printf 'if then\n' >"$W/c-parse.sh"
    note "control: the same parse refuses a broken if" "$(isnot parse_ok "$W/c-parse.sh")"
    echo "command: python3 --version"
    python3 --version 2>&1 | sed 's/^/    /'
    py_compiles() { python3 -c 'import py_compile, sys; py_compile.compile(sys.argv[1], cfile=sys.argv[2], doraise=True)' "$1" "$W/compiled.pyc" 2>/dev/null; }
    while IFS= read -r s; do
      case "$s" in
        *.py)
          git show "$C:$s" >"$W/compiled.py"
          note "$s compiles at the phase commit (py_compile, doraise)" "$(is py_compiles "$W/compiled.py")"
          npyall=$((npyall + 1)) ;;
      esac
    done <"$W/scripts-all"
    echo "  shell scripts parsed: $nsh; Python scripts compiled: $npyall"
    both_read() { [ "$nsh" -ge 1 ] && [ "$npyall" -ge 1 ]; }
    note "some shell scripts and some Python scripts were read" "$(is both_read)"
    printf 'def f(:\n    pass\n' >"$W/c-broken.py"
    note "control: the same compile refuses a broken def" "$(isnot py_compiles "$W/c-broken.py")"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '[.]py$' "$W/difffiles" >"$W/py-in-diff" || :
    : >"$W/py-in-diff-want"
    echo "  Python scripts in the phase diff: $(count_lines "$W/py-in-diff")"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$W/py-in-diff"
    note "no Python script is in the phase diff (changes H43 to H45)" "$(is cmp -s "$W/py-in-diff" "$W/py-in-diff-want")"
    printf 'scripts/scale-gen.py\n' >"$W/c-py-one"
    note "control: the comparison refuses a list of one" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/c-py-one" "$W/py-in-diff-want")"
    printf 'scripts/scale-gen.py\ncrates/emend/src/package.rs\n' >"$W/c-py"
    ctl "one Python script in a list of two, same command form" 1 count_matches -E '[.]py$' "$W/c-py"
    
    echo
    echo "## the new sources scored against the gate they must pass, with controls"
    OFF=$(git show "$C:scripts/check.sh" | sed -n "s/^readonly OFFICE_RE='\(.*\)'\$/\1/p")
    note "OFFICE_RE was read from check.sh and is non-empty" "$(is [ -n "$OFF" ])"
    PRE_COMMIT=$(git log --format='%H' --grep='^T0 P6d: narrow the three path patterns' -n 1)
    note "the P6d narrowing commit resolved from git" "$(is [ -n "$PRE_COMMIT" ])"
    git show "$PRE_COMMIT^:scripts/privacy-patterns.txt" >"$W/pre-all" 2>/dev/null || fail=1
    sed -n '8p;10p;11p' "$W/pre-all" >"$W/pre-patterns"
    note "three pre-P6d forms read from the narrowing commit's parent" \
      "$(is [ "$(count_lines "$W/pre-patterns")" = 3 ])"
    git show "$C:scripts/privacy-patterns.txt" >"$W/live-patterns"
    
    f_nonascii() { count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$1"; }
    f_ctrl()     { count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$1"; }
    f_live()     { count_from_file -E "$W/live-patterns" "$1"; }
    f_pre()      { count_from_file -E "$W/pre-patterns" "$1"; }
    f_office()   { count_matches -E "$OFF" "$1"; }
    # P1 gate header change 7, kept: an office extension whose file name is a literal, the
    # name running back from the extension to a space, a quote, a slash, an
    # equals sign or the line's start with no shell expansion in it.
    f_office_literal() { count_matches -E "(^|[ \"'=/])[^ \"'=/\$]+$OFF" "$1"; }
    
    rep() { printf "$1%.0s" $(seq 1 "$2"); }
    printf 'plain\nhas \303\251 byte\n' >"$W/c-nonascii"
    printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m\017 y\n' >"$W/c-ctrl"
    printf 'x %s%s%s y\n' 'gh' 'p_' "$(rep a 24)" >"$W/c-live"
    printf 'x %s%s%s y\n' '/mnt/' 'c/' 'Users/' >"$W/c-pre"
    printf 'name.%s%s\n' 'xl' 'sx' >"$W/c-office"
    printf 'input=$KEEP/$test.in.%s%s\n' 'xl' 'sx' >"$W/c-office-expanded"
    printf 'plain ascii only\n' >"$W/c-clean"
    ctl "f_nonascii on a two-byte character" 2 f_nonascii "$W/c-nonascii"
    ctl "f_ctrl on ESC, ESC and SI" 3 f_ctrl "$W/c-ctrl"
    ctl "f_live on a token shape" 1 f_live "$W/c-live"
    ctl "f_pre on a bare path shape" 1 f_pre "$W/c-pre"
    ctl "f_office on an office file name" 1 f_office "$W/c-office"
    ctl "f_office_literal on the same literal name" 1 f_office_literal "$W/c-office"
    ctl "f_office on a name built from variables" 1 f_office "$W/c-office-expanded"
    ctl "f_office_literal on the same built name" 0 f_office_literal "$W/c-office-expanded"
    for f in f_nonascii f_ctrl f_live f_pre f_office f_office_literal; do
      ctl "$f on a clean file" 0 "$f" "$W/c-clean"
    done
    clean_source() {
      [ "$(f_nonascii "$1")" = 0 ] && [ "$(f_ctrl "$1")" = 0 ] &&
        [ "$(f_live "$1")" = 0 ] && [ "$(f_pre "$1")" = 0 ] && [ "$(f_office_literal "$1")" = 0 ]
    }
    
    git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A "$BASE" "$C" >"$W/added"
    echo "  files added in this phase: $(count_lines "$W/added")"
    nscored=0
    while IFS= read -r s; do
      git show "$C:$s" >"$W/a-at-head" 2>/dev/null || { echo "$s: READ ERROR"; fail=1; continue; }
      echo "$s (new in this phase):"
      echo "  non-ASCII bytes: $(f_nonascii "$W/a-at-head")"
      echo "  control bytes: $(f_ctrl "$W/a-at-head")"
      echo "  hits against all $(count_lines "$W/live-patterns") live privacy patterns: $(f_live "$W/a-at-head")"
      echo "  hits against the three pre-P6d bare forms: $(f_pre "$W/a-at-head")"
      echo "  lines with an office extension: $(f_office "$W/a-at-head"); of them a literal file name: $(f_office_literal "$W/a-at-head")"
      note "$s is clean on the five forms, office names counted as literals" "$(is clean_source "$W/a-at-head")"
      nscored=$((nscored + 1))
    done <"$W/added"
    
    echo
    echo "## the files this phase MODIFIED, scored by change rather than absolutely"
    git diff --name-only --diff-filter=M "$BASE" "$C" >"$W/modified"
    echo "  files modified in this phase: $(count_lines "$W/modified")"
    unchanged_by_this_phase() {
      [ "$added" = 0 ] && [ "$at_base" != error ] && [ "$at_head" != error ] &&
        [ "$at_base" = "$at_head" ]
    }
    while IFS= read -r M; do
      git show "$BASE:$M" >"$W/m-at-base" 2>/dev/null || { echo "$M: READ ERROR at base"; fail=1; continue; }
      git show "$C:$M" >"$W/m-at-head" 2>/dev/null || { echo "$M: READ ERROR at the phase commit"; fail=1; continue; }
      git diff -U0 "$BASE" "$C" -- "$M" |
        LC_ALL=C "$G" '^+' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -v '^+++' | sed 's/^+//' >"$W/m-added"
      echo "$M (modified in this phase):"
      echo "  added lines: $(count_lines "$W/m-added")"
      for form in f_nonascii f_ctrl f_live f_pre f_office_literal f_office; do
        at_base=$("$form" "$W/m-at-base")
        added=$("$form" "$W/m-added")
        at_head=$("$form" "$W/m-at-head")
        echo "  $form: at the base $at_base, in the added lines $added, at the phase commit $at_head"
        if [ "$form" = f_office ]; then
          # Printed only: a moved or rebuilt line can lower the count, and the
          # literal form above is the one held to "nothing new".
          continue
        fi
        note "$M: $form introduces nothing new in this phase" "$(is unchanged_by_this_phase)"
      done
      nscored=$((nscored + 1))
    done <"$W/modified"
    
    echo
    echo "## every file in the diff was scored"
    ndiff=$(count_lines "$W/difffiles")
    echo "  files in the diff: $ndiff; files scored as new or modified: $nscored"
    note "every file in the phase diff was scored" "$(is [ "$ndiff" = "$nscored" ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the public fn and const first lines, equal to the base's, a file's items taking the cfg line of its mod declaration (change E36; P3's E35, P2's E34, P1's E33, M3 part 5 P2's E31, P1's E30, M3 part 4 P1's E28, M3 part 3 P3's E26 reader, M2 part 4c P2's E12, part 4b P1's E7 and part 4a P4's D5, kept)"
    # The first line of every "pub fn" and "pub const" in crates/emend/src outside
    # the test files, leading space, "mut " before a parameter and a trailing brace
    # dropped, each beside the attribute before it when the line before is one
    # ("#[...", an attribute over several lines joined into one line, change
    # E26), else "-", sorted by the first line. Change E31: an item with neither
    # its own cfg line nor a gated impl's takes the cfg line of its file's mod
    # declaration in the parent file, when that line is one. Change E38: this
    # phase's two package.rs lines sit inside a private fn and add no public
    # item, so the list is the base's, and every cfg line's items are the base's.
    # file_gate <commit> <path>: the line before the path's mod declaration in
    # its parent file (crates/emend/src/a/b.rs: `mod b;` in crates/emend/src/a.rs)
    # when that line is a feature cfg line, else nothing (change E31).
    file_gate() {
      local at=$1 f=$2 dir name
      case "$f" in crates/emend/src/*/*.rs) ;; *) return 0 ;; esac
      dir=${f%/*}; name=${f##*/}; name=${name%.rs}
      git show "$at:$dir.rs" 2>/dev/null | awk -v m="mod $name;" '$0 == m { print p; exit } { p = $0 }' |
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^#\[cfg\(feature = "[a-z]+"\)\]$' || :
    }
    pub_with_attrs() {
      local at=$1 f
      for f in $(git ls-tree -r --name-only "$at" -- crates/emend/src | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '[.]rs$' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vE '(/tests[.]rs|/testing[.]rs|/tests/)'); do
        git show "$at:$f" | awk -v filecfg="$(file_gate "$at" "$f")" '
          function trimmed(s) { sub(/^[[:space:]]*/, "", s); return s }
          function joined(s) { gsub(/[(] /, "(", s); gsub(/ [)]/, ")", s); return s }
          # Change E26: an attribute over several lines, from its "#[" line to
          # the line ending "]", is one line, a space between its pieces and
          # none just inside a parenthesis.
          inattr { attr = attr " " trimmed($0); if ($0 ~ /\]$/) { inattr = 0; prev = joined(attr) }; next }
          /^[[:space:]]*#\[/ && $0 !~ /\]$/ { inattr = 1; attr = trimmed($0); next }
          # Change D5, kept and widened by E7: an impl whose own attribute line is
          # a feature cfg gates every pub fn inside it with that line, up to the
          # impl'"'"'s closing brace at the margin.
          # Change E31: outside a gated impl, the gate of the file itself.
          BEGIN { gated = filecfg }
          /^impl/ { gated = (prev ~ /^#\[cfg\(feature = "[a-z]+"\)\]$/) ? prev : filecfg }
          /^}/ { gated = filecfg }
          /^[[:space:]]*pub (fn|const) / {
            line = $0; sub(/^[[:space:]]*/, "", line); sub(/ [{]$/, "", line)
            gsub(/[(]mut /, "(", line); gsub(/, mut /, ", ", line)
            a = prev; sub(/^[[:space:]]*/, "", a)
            if (a !~ /^#\[/) a = (gated != "" ? gated : "-")
            print a "\t" line
          }
          { prev = $0 }'
      done | LC_ALL=C sort -t "$(printf '\t')" -k2
    }
    TAB=$(printf '\t')
    READ_CFG='#[cfg(feature = "read")]'
    COMMENTS_CFG='#[cfg(feature = "comments")]'
    IMAGES_CFG='#[cfg(feature = "images")]'
    METADATA_CFG='#[cfg(feature = "metadata")]'
    COPY_CFG='#[cfg(feature = "copy")]'
    COMMENTS_ANY='#[cfg(any(feature = "comments", feature = "copy"))]'
    METADATA_ANY='#[cfg(any(feature = "metadata", feature = "copy"))]'
    PAIR_CFG='#[cfg(all(feature = "sheetprops", feature = "metadata"))]'
    TABLE_NEW='#[cfg(any(feature = "rowcol", feature = "tables", all(feature = "sheetprops", feature = "metadata")))]'
    echo "command: git show <commit>:<each crates/emend/src/*.rs outside the tests> | awk (a pub fn or pub const first line, beside the previous line when it is an attribute, one over several lines joined), sorted, at the base and at the phase commit"
    pub_with_attrs "$BASE" >"$W/pubattr-base"
    pub_with_attrs "$C" >"$W/pubattr-head"
    echo "  at the phase commit, every pub fn and pub const first line with its attribute:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$W/pubattr-head"
    cut -f2 "$W/pubattr-base" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$W/pub-base"
    cut -f2 "$W/pubattr-head" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$W/pub-on"
    echo "  pub first lines: at the base $(count_lines "$W/pub-base"); at the phase commit $(count_lines "$W/pub-on")"
    LC_ALL=C comm -13 "$W/pub-base" "$W/pub-on" >"$W/pub-new"
    LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$W/pub-base" "$W/pub-on" >"$W/pub-lost"
    echo "  the lines the base's list loses at the phase commit:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$W/pub-lost"
    echo "  the lines the phase commit's list adds to the base's:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$W/pub-new"
    # Change L45: the range changes doc lines alone in lib.rs, so the list is the
    # base's.
    note "the phase commit's pub fn and const first lines are the base's (change L45)" "$(is cmp -s "$W/pub-base" "$W/pub-on")"
    note "some first lines were read" "$(is [ "$(count_lines "$W/pub-on")" -ge 1 ])"
    sed '1d' "$W/pub-on" >"$W/c-pub-on-short"
    note "control: the same comparison refuses the phase commit's list one line short" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/pub-base" "$W/c-pub-on-short")"
    gated_by() {
      awk -F "$TAB" -v cfg="$2" '$1 == cfg { print $2 }' "$1" |
        sed -E 's/^pub (fn|const) ([A-Za-z_0-9]+).*/\1 \2/' | LC_ALL=C sort
    }
    # Change E36: P3's items stand where P3 put them: copy_sheet under the copy
    # cfg line, COMMENTS and HYPERLINK under the lines adding copy.
    gated_by "$W/pubattr-head" "$COPY_CFG" >"$W/gated-copy"
    printf 'fn copy_sheet\n' >"$W/gated-copy-want"
    echo "  under $COPY_CFG at the phase commit: $(tr '\n' ' ' <"$W/gated-copy")"
    echo "  under $COMMENTS_ANY at the phase commit: $(gated_by "$W/pubattr-head" "$COMMENTS_ANY" | tr '\n' ' ')"
    echo "  under $METADATA_ANY at the phase commit: $(gated_by "$W/pubattr-head" "$METADATA_ANY" | tr '\n' ' ')"
    note "the item under the copy cfg line is copy_sheet alone (change E36)" "$(is cmp -s "$W/gated-copy" "$W/gated-copy-want")"
    note "COMMENTS alone stands under the cfg line adding copy to comments (change E36)" "$(is [ "$(gated_by "$W/pubattr-head" "$COMMENTS_ANY")" = "const COMMENTS" ])"
    note "HYPERLINK alone stands under the cfg line adding copy to metadata (change E36)" "$(is [ "$(gated_by "$W/pubattr-head" "$METADATA_ANY")" = "const HYPERLINK" ])"
    echo "  file_gate at the phase commit: package/sheet_read.rs '$(file_gate "$C" crates/emend/src/package/sheet_read.rs)'; styles/elements.rs '$(file_gate "$C" crates/emend/src/styles/elements.rs)'; package.rs '$(file_gate "$C" crates/emend/src/package.rs)'"
    note "file_gate gives package/sheet_read.rs the read cfg line (M3 part 5 P2's E31)" "$(is [ "$(file_gate "$C" crates/emend/src/package/sheet_read.rs)" = "$READ_CFG" ])"
    note "control: file_gate gives an ungated module (styles/elements.rs) nothing" "$(is [ -z "$(file_gate "$C" crates/emend/src/styles/elements.rs)" ])"
    note "control: file_gate gives a top-level file (package.rs) nothing" "$(is [ -z "$(file_gate "$C" crates/emend/src/package.rs)" ])"
    # M3 part 1 P1's E18 form: the items of every other cfg line the list carries
    # are the base's, item for item; P3's two-feature line, TABLE's widened line,
    # the read line, the images line and the copy lines among them (changes E33,
    # E35 and E36): with no public item added, every cfg line is compared.
    awk -F "$TAB" '$1 ~ /^#\[cfg\(/ { print $1 }' "$W/pubattr-head" | LC_ALL=C sort -u >"$W/cfgs"
    echo "  the other cfg lines the list carries at the phase commit:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$W/cfgs"
    note "the list carries other cfg lines, some" "$(is [ "$(count_lines "$W/cfgs")" -ge 1 ])"
    note "P3's two-feature cfg line is among them" "$(is [ "$(count_matches -Fx "$PAIR_CFG" "$W/cfgs")" = 1 ])"
    note "TABLE's widened cfg line is among them" "$(is [ "$(count_matches -Fx "$TABLE_NEW" "$W/cfgs")" = 1 ])"
    note "the read cfg line is among them (change E33)" "$(is [ "$(count_matches -Fx "$READ_CFG" "$W/cfgs")" = 1 ])"
    note "the images cfg line is among them (change E35)" "$(is [ "$(count_matches -Fx "$IMAGES_CFG" "$W/cfgs")" = 1 ])"
    note "the copy cfg line is among them (change E36)" "$(is [ "$(count_matches -Fx "$COPY_CFG" "$W/cfgs")" = 1 ])"
    while IFS= read -r cfg; do
      gated_by "$W/pubattr-head" "$cfg" >"$W/gated-head"
      gated_by "$W/pubattr-base" "$cfg" >"$W/gated-base"
      echo "  $cfg: items at the base $(count_lines "$W/gated-base"), at the phase commit $(count_lines "$W/gated-head")"
      note "the items under $cfg are the base's, item for item" "$(is cmp -s "$W/gated-head" "$W/gated-base")"
    done <"$W/cfgs"
    printf '%s\n' 'pub fn planted(&self)' >"$W/c-pub-extra"
    note "control: the comparison refuses a list one call long" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/c-pub-extra" "$W/pub-new-want")"
    : >"$W/c-gated-short"
    note "control: the copy comparison refuses a list one item short" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/gated-copy" "$W/c-gated-short")"
    printf '%s\n' "    $PAIR_CFG" '    pub fn x(&self) {' '    /// doc' '    pub const Y: u8 = 1;' >"$W/c-attr.rs"
    c_attr() {
      awk '
        /^[[:space:]]*pub (fn|const) / { a = prev; sub(/^[[:space:]]*/, "", a); if (a !~ /^#\[/) a = "-"; print a }
        { prev = $0 }' "$W/c-attr.rs" | tr '\n' '|'
    }
    c_attr_ok() { [ "$(c_attr)" = "$PAIR_CFG|-|" ]; }
    note "control: the attribute reader pairs a cfg line with the fn after it and a doc line with '-'" "$(is c_attr_ok)"
    # Change E26's control: the joining reader over a fixture holding TABLE's
    # six-line cfg, a one-line one and a doc line.
    printf '%s\n' '#[cfg(any(' '    feature = "rowcol",' '    feature = "tables",' '    all(feature = "sheetprops", feature = "metadata")' '))]' 'pub const T: u8 = 1;' "$PAIR_CFG" 'pub fn f(&self) {}' '/// doc' 'pub fn g(&self) {}' >"$W/c-multi.rs"
    c_multi() {
      awk '
        function trimmed(s) { sub(/^[[:space:]]*/, "", s); return s }
        function joined(s) { gsub(/[(] /, "(", s); gsub(/ [)]/, ")", s); return s }
        inattr { attr = attr " " trimmed($0); if ($0 ~ /\]$/) { inattr = 0; prev = joined(attr) }; next }
        /^[[:space:]]*#\[/ && $0 !~ /\]$/ { inattr = 1; attr = trimmed($0); next }
        /^[[:space:]]*pub (fn|const) / { a = prev; sub(/^[[:space:]]*/, "", a); if (a !~ /^#\[/) a = "-"; print a }
        { prev = $0 }' "$W/c-multi.rs" | tr '\n' '|'
    }
    c_multi_ok() { [ "$(c_multi)" = "$TABLE_NEW|$PAIR_CFG|-|" ]; }
    note "control: the reader joins a six-line attribute into the widened cfg line and keeps one-line attributes and doc lines (change E26)" "$(is c_multi_ok)"
    # Change D5's control, widened by E7: the reader itself, over a fixture with
    # a gated impl and an ungated one, gives the pub fn inside the gated impl the
    # cfg line.
    FEATURE_CFG='#[cfg(feature = "sheetprops")]'
    printf '%s\n' "$FEATURE_CFG" 'impl A {' '    /// doc' '    pub fn inside(&self) {}' '}' 'impl B {' '    /// doc' '    pub fn outside(&self) {}' '}' >"$W/c-impl.rs"
    c_impl() {
      awk '
        /^impl/ { gated = (prev ~ /^#\[cfg\(feature = "[a-z]+"\)\]$/) ? prev : "" }
        /^}/ { gated = "" }
        /^[[:space:]]*pub (fn|const) / { a = prev; sub(/^[[:space:]]*/, "", a); if (a !~ /^#\[/) a = (gated != "" ? gated : "-"); print a }
        { prev = $0 }' "$W/c-impl.rs" | tr '\n' '|'
    }
    c_impl_ok() { [ "$(c_impl)" = "$FEATURE_CFG|-|" ]; }
    note "control: the reader gives a pub fn in a gated impl the cfg line and one in an ungated impl '-' (change D5)" "$(is c_impl_ok)"
    nunsafe=$(git grep -c -w -e unsafe "$C" -- crates/emend/src | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }')
    nforbid=$(git show "$C:crates/emend/src/lib.rs" | count_matches -Fx '#![forbid(unsafe_code)]' /dev/stdin)
    echo "  lines holding the word unsafe under crates/emend/src at the phase commit: $nunsafe; lib.rs's forbid line: $nforbid"
    note "lib.rs still forbids unsafe code" "$(is [ "$nforbid" = 1 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the base's tests: no test file in the range, none edited or gone; the test names of the whole tree the base's (change F6, kept; changes F35, I38 to I40, I43 and I44)"
    git diff --name-only "$BASE" "$C" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '(/tests[.]rs|/tests/|^tools/.*/tests/)' >"$W/test-files" || :
    sed 's/^/    test file changed: /' "$W/test-files"
    # test_bodies <commit> <file>: "<name>\t<body with each line joined by a
    # form feed>" per #[test] fn, the body from the fn line to the first line
    # that is a closing brace at the left margin.
    test_bodies() {
      python3 - "$1" "$2" <<'BODIES'
    import re, subprocess, sys
    at, path = sys.argv[1:3]
    if subprocess.run(["git", "cat-file", "-e", at + "^{commit}"], capture_output=True).returncode != 0:
        sys.exit("no such commit")
    if subprocess.run(["git", "cat-file", "-e", f"{at}:{path}"], capture_output=True).returncode != 0:
        sys.exit(0)
    text = subprocess.run(["git", "show", f"{at}:{path}"], capture_output=True, text=True,
                          check=True).stdout.split("\n")
    i = 0
    while i < len(text):
        if text[i].strip() == "#[test]":
            j = i + 1
            while j < len(text) and not re.match(r"^\s*fn ", text[j]):
                j += 1
            if j >= len(text):
                break
            name = re.match(r"^\s*fn ([a-z0-9_]+)", text[j]).group(1)
            k = j
            while k < len(text) and text[k] != "}":
                k += 1
            print(name + "\t" + "\f".join(text[j:k + 1]))
            i = k
        i += 1
    BODIES
    }
    # added_in <base bodies> <head bodies> <file>: per base test, "gone", or one
    # line "<file> <test> - <line, stripped>" per line removed from its body and
    # "<file> <test> + <line, stripped>" per line added, by a line diff of the
    # body at the base against the body now (change I4).
    added_in() {
      python3 - "$1" "$2" "$3" <<'ADDED'
    import difflib, sys
    base = dict(l.rstrip("\n").split("\t", 1) for l in open(sys.argv[1]) if l.strip())
    head = dict(l.rstrip("\n").split("\t", 1) for l in open(sys.argv[2]) if l.strip())
    for name, body in sorted(base.items()):
        if name not in head:
            print("%s %s gone" % (sys.argv[3], name))
            continue
        old, new = body.split("\f"), head[name].split("\f")
        for tag, i1, i2, j1, j2 in difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, old, new, autojunk=False).get_opcodes():
            if tag in ("replace", "delete"):
                for line in old[i1:i2]:
                    print("%s %s - %s" % (sys.argv[3], name, line.strip()))
            if tag in ("replace", "insert"):
                for line in new[j1:j2]:
                    print("%s %s + %s" % (sys.argv[3], name, line.strip()))
    ADDED
    }
    : >"$W/tests-edited"; tb_fail=0
    nbase_tests=0
    while IFS= read -r tf; do
      test_bodies "$BASE" "$tf" >"$W/tb-base" || tb_fail=1
      test_bodies "$C" "$tf" >"$W/tb-head" || tb_fail=1
      nbase_tests=$((nbase_tests + $(count_lines "$W/tb-base")))
      added_in "$W/tb-base" "$W/tb-head" "$tf" >>"$W/tests-edited" || tb_fail=1
    done <"$W/test-files"
    echo "command: every #[test] fn of the base in each changed test file, read at the base and at the phase commit; the lines removed from it and added to it, by a line diff, and any gone"
    echo "  base tests read in the changed files: $nbase_tests"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$W/tests-edited"
    LC_ALL=C sort "$W/tests-edited" >"$W/tests-edited-sorted"
    # Change I44: no test file is in the phase diff, so no base test is edited
    # or gone; the names of every test in the tree are the base's.
    PKG_TESTS=crates/emend/src/package/tests.rs
    ngone=$(count_matches -E ' gone$' "$W/tests-edited")
    nedit=$(count_lines "$W/tests-edited")
    note "every test of the base and the phase commit was read, none failing" "$(is [ "$tb_fail" = 0 ])"
    echo "  test files in the phase diff: $(count_lines "$W/test-files")"
    note "no test file is in the phase diff (change I44)" "$(is [ "$(count_lines "$W/test-files")" = 0 ])"
    printf 'crates/emend/src/package/tests.rs\nscripts/counting.sh\n' >"$W/c-test-files"
    ctl "test files in a planted list of two, the same pattern" 1 count_matches -E '(/tests[.]rs|/tests/|^tools/.*/tests/)' "$W/c-test-files"
    note "no test of the base is gone ($ngone)" "$(is [ "$ngone" = 0 ])"
    note "no line of a base test is edited ($nedit) (change I44)" "$(is [ "$nedit" = 0 ])"
    printf '%s\n' 'x.rs t gone' 'x.rs u - let a = 1;' >"$W/c-edited"
    ctl "a gone test in a list, same command form" 1 count_matches -E ' gone$' "$W/c-edited"
    ctl "edit lines in a planted list of two, same command form" 2 count_lines "$W/c-edited"
    # The test names of the whole tree: every #[test] fn in every Rust file under
    # crates/ and tools/, as a sorted list of "<file> <name>", at the base and at
    # the phase commit.
    tree_test_names() {
      local at=$1 f
      for f in $(git ls-tree -r --name-only "$at" -- crates tools | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '[.]rs$'); do
        test_bodies "$at" "$f" | cut -f1 | sed "s#^#$f #"
      done | LC_ALL=C sort
    }
    tree_test_names "$BASE" >"$W/names-base"
    tree_test_names "$C" >"$W/names-head"
    echo "command: every #[test] fn's name in every .rs file under crates/ and tools/, read by the same reader at the base and at the phase commit, sorted"
    echo "  test names at the base: $(count_lines "$W/names-base"); at the phase commit: $(count_lines "$W/names-head")"
    LC_ALL=C diff "$W/names-base" "$W/names-head" | sed 's/^/    /' || :
    note "the test names of the whole tree are the base's (change I43)" "$(is cmp -s "$W/names-base" "$W/names-head")"
    note "some test names were read" "$(is [ "$(count_lines "$W/names-head")" -ge 1 ])"
    sed '1d' "$W/names-head" >"$W/c-names-short"
    note "control: the comparison refuses the list one name short" "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/names-base" "$W/c-names-short")"
    gated_line_before() {
      git show "$C:$PKG_TESTS" | awk '
        /^fn a_local_sheet_id_that_is_not_a_number_refuses_a_move_at_the_write[(]/ { print p2 "|" p1; exit }
        { p2 = p1; p1 = $0 }'
    }
    echo "  the two lines before part 1's test's fn line at the phase commit: $(gated_line_before)"
    gated_ok() { [ "$(gated_line_before)" = '#[cfg(not(feature = "metadata"))]|#[test]' ]; }
    note "part 1's test at the write is still gated to the feature off" "$(is gated_ok)"
    STY_TESTS=crates/emend/src/styles/tests.rs
    counts_gate_before() {
      git show "$1:$STY_TESTS" | awk '
        /^fn the_counts_are_the_children_not_the_count_attribute[(]/ { print p2 "|" p1; exit }
        { p2 = p1; p1 = $0 }'
    }
    echo "  the two lines before the core count test's fn line at the phase commit: $(counts_gate_before "$C")"
    counts_gated_ok() { [ "$(counts_gate_before "$1")" = '#[cfg(not(feature = "read"))]|#[test]' ]; }
    note "the core count test is still gated to the feature read off (M3 part 5 P1's F30)" "$(is counts_gated_ok "$C")"
    PRE_P1=$(git log --format='%H' -n 1 --grep='^M3 part 4 close-out record:')
    echo "  the record commit before M3 part 5 P1, by subject: ${PRE_P1:-none found}; the two lines there: $(counts_gate_before "$PRE_P1")"
    note "control: the same reader refuses the commit before P1, where the test was not gated" "$(isnot counts_gated_ok "$PRE_P1")"
    
    echo
    echo "## full run on the phase's main-tree target directory, started from / by absolute path, its doc directory removed first (changes J35, K35 and L40)"
    echo "  CARGO_TARGET_DIR: <target>/main; rulings 8 and 10 share it across the phase's dry and logged runs of <repo>, so no cargo clean runs and the cache is warm, but <target>/main/doc goes before every doc build (specs/0029 P3 verification ruling 2)"
    # Change L40: <target>/main/doc, printed as there or not, removed by rm -r
    # without -f when there, and checked gone, before every doc build.
    DOC_DIR=$MAIN_TARGET/doc
    doc_gone() { [ ! -e "$DOC_DIR" ]; }
    doc_fresh() {
      if [ -d "$DOC_DIR" ]; then
        echo "  <target>/main/doc is there: yes"
        echo "command: rm -r <target>/main/doc"
        rm -r "${DOC_DIR:?}" </dev/null
        echo "    rm -r exit $?"
      else
        echo "  <target>/main/doc is there: no"
      fi
      note "<target>/main/doc is gone before the doc build (change L40)" "$(is doc_gone)"
    }
    doc_gone_ctl() { local DOC_DIR=$MAIN_TARGET; doc_gone; }
    note "control: doc_gone refuses a directory that is there (<target>/main)" "$(isnot doc_gone_ctl)"
    doc_fresh
    GATE=$MAIN/scripts/check.sh
    echo "command: (cd / && <repo>/scripts/check.sh)"
    ( cd / && RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 "$GATE" ) >"$W/gate.out" 2>"$W/gate.err"
    grc=$?
    sed 's/^/    /' "$W/gate.out"
    echo "exit: $grc; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$W/gate.err")"
    npass=$(count_matches -E '^PASS ' "$W/gate.out")
    ndoc_step=$(count_matches -E '^PASS doc$' "$W/gate.out")
    note "the gate exits 0" "$(is [ "$grc" -eq 0 ])"
    note "nine PASS lines" "$(is [ "$npass" = 9 ])"
    note "the doc step is one of them, by name" "$(is [ "$ndoc_step" = 1 ])"
    note "stderr is empty" "$(is [ "$(wc -c <"$W/gate.err")" -eq 0 ])"
    # The full gate prints nothing of its doc step but its PASS line; its
    # cargo doc --workspace writes <target>/main/doc again, removed above.
    index_there() { [ -s "$DOC_DIR/emend/all.html" ]; }
    echo "  <target>/main/doc/emend/all.html after the full gate: $([ -s "$DOC_DIR/emend/all.html" ] && echo "there, $(wc -c <"$DOC_DIR/emend/all.html") bytes" || echo "not there")"
    note "the full gate's doc step wrote the index again after the directory was removed (change L40)" "$(is index_there)"
    index_ctl() { local DOC_DIR=$W/no-such-doc; index_there; }
    note "control: index_there refuses a directory that does not exist" "$(isnot index_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## the binaries the gate built, both targets: the DEBUG builds of emend-copy and xlsx-diff, host and i686 (the later logs of this phase read the two emend-copy hashes against these lines)"
    bins_ok=yes
    for b in "$CARGO_TARGET_DIR"/debug/emend-copy "$CARGO_TARGET_DIR"/debug/xlsx-diff \
             "$CARGO_TARGET_DIR"/i686-unknown-linux-musl/debug/emend-copy \
             "$CARGO_TARGET_DIR"/i686-unknown-linux-musl/debug/xlsx-diff; do
      if [ -x "$b" ]; then
        echo "  $b: sha256 $(sha256sum <"$b" | cut -d' ' -f1), bytes $(wc -c <"$b")"
      else
        echo "  $b: MISSING or not executable"
        bins_ok=no
      fi
    done
    note "the gate left all four binaries, both targets, executable" "$(is [ "$bins_ok" = yes ])"
    # Change J35 (c): a later log may rebuild into the shared target, so the
    # negative log reads the gate's binaries from copies kept under <build>
    # (changes K39 to K43 and K44: the copies stay as the carried form).
    mkdir -p "$BUILD_ROOT/bin/host" "$BUILD_ROOT/bin/i686" || fail=1
    echo "command: cp each DEBUG binary above into <build>/bin/host or <build>/bin/i686 under its own name; sha256sum each copy"
    copies_ok=yes
    for pair in "host:$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/debug" "i686:$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/i686-unknown-linux-musl/debug"; do
      label=${pair%%:*}; dir=${pair#*:}
      for name in emend-copy xlsx-diff; do
        cp "$dir/$name" "$BUILD_ROOT/bin/$label/$name" || copies_ok=no
        a=$(sha256sum <"$dir/$name" | cut -d' ' -f1)
        b=$(sha256sum <"$BUILD_ROOT/bin/$label/$name" | cut -d' ' -f1)
        echo "  <build>/bin/$label/$name: sha256 $b, bytes $(wc -c <"$BUILD_ROOT/bin/$label/$name")"
        [ "$a" = "$b" ] || copies_ok=no
      done
    done
    note "each copy is executable and hashes as the binary it copies" "$(is [ "$copies_ok" = yes ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## clippy and doc with the features off, copy alone, comments alone, the two together, and every feature, and clippy over the probe crate's feature sets, copy and copy with comments among them (change H4, kept; changes G6, G16, G21, G24, G26, G28, G29, G30, G31, G33, G34, G35 and G36)"
    # Changes J35 (b) and K35: the main tree's target directory for every run of
    # <repo>.
    FEAT_TARGET=$MAIN_TARGET
    PROBE_TARGET=$MAIN_TARGET
    diag_lines() { count_matches -E '^(warning|error)(\[|:)' "$1"; }
    lint_clean() { [ "$1" = 0 ] && [ "$2" = 0 ]; }
    lint_run() {
      local label=$1 dir=$2 rc n
      shift 2
      echo "command: ${LINT_SHOWN}"
      ( cd "$MAIN" && RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$dir "$@" ) >"$W/lint.out" 2>&1
      rc=$?
      n=$(diag_lines "$W/lint.out")
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -E '^(warning|error)(\[|:)' "$W/lint.out" | sed 's/^/    /'
      echo "  $label: exit $rc; warning or error lines $n"
      note "$label is clean: exit 0 and no warning or error line" "$(is lint_clean "$rc" "$n")"
    }
    LINT_SHOWN="CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main cargo clippy -p emend --all-targets -- -D warnings"
    lint_run "clippy, the crate, feature off" "$FEAT_TARGET" cargo clippy -p emend --all-targets -- -D warnings
    for fs in copy comments copy,comments; do
      LINT_SHOWN="CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main cargo clippy -p emend --all-targets --features $fs -- -D warnings"
      lint_run "clippy, the crate, features $fs" "$FEAT_TARGET" cargo clippy -p emend --all-targets --features "$fs" -- -D warnings
    done
    LINT_SHOWN="CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main cargo clippy -p emend --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings"
    lint_run "clippy, the crate, every feature on" "$FEAT_TARGET" cargo clippy -p emend --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
    # Change L40: each doc build after doc_fresh, and its output holding a
    # line "Documenting emend", so rustdoc ran in this log.
    documenting_seen() { [ "$(count_matches -E '^ *Documenting emend ' "$1")" -ge 1 ]; }
    doc_run() {
      local label=$1
      shift
      doc_fresh
      lint_run "$label" "$FEAT_TARGET" "$@"
      echo "  lines of the build's output reading \"Documenting emend\": $(count_matches -E '^ *Documenting emend ' "$W/lint.out")"
      note "$label: rustdoc ran (\"Documenting emend\" in cargo's output; change L40)" "$(is documenting_seen "$W/lint.out")"
    }
    LINT_SHOWN="RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main cargo doc -p emend --no-deps"
    doc_run "doc, the crate, feature off" env RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc -p emend --no-deps
    for fs in copy comments copy,comments; do
      LINT_SHOWN="RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main cargo doc -p emend --no-deps --features $fs"
      doc_run "doc, the crate, features $fs" env RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc -p emend --no-deps --features "$fs"
    done
    LINT_SHOWN="RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main cargo doc -p emend --no-deps --all-features"
    doc_run "doc, the crate, every feature on" env RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc -p emend --no-deps --all-features
    printf '    Finished `dev` profile [unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 0.05s\n   Generated /x/doc/emend/index.html\n' >"$W/c-doc-fresh"
    printf '    Checking emend v0.1.0\n Documenting emend v0.1.0 (/x)\n    Finished `dev` profile\n' >"$W/c-doc-ran"
    note "control: documenting_seen refuses an output holding only Finished and Generated (P3's 0.05 s case)" "$(isnot documenting_seen "$W/c-doc-fresh")"
    note "control: documenting_seen accepts an output holding the line" "$(is documenting_seen "$W/c-doc-ran")"
    # Change L40 (P3 verification ruling 3): the every-feature index's item
    # links, the section anchors (links to "#...") excluded.
    ALL_HTML=$DOC_DIR/emend/all.html
    echo "command: grep -o -E '<li><a href=\"[^\"]*\"' <target>/main/doc/emend/all.html; the links counted, those to \"#...\" (the section anchors) and the others (the items)"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E '<li><a href="[^"]*"' "$ALL_HTML" >"$W/all-links" 2>/dev/null || :
    nlinks=$(count_lines "$W/all-links")
    nanchors=$(count_matches -E 'href="#' "$W/all-links")
    nitems=$(count_matches -E 'href="[^#"]' "$W/all-links")
    echo "  links: $nlinks; section anchors: $nanchors; item links: $nitems"
    echo "  item links by kind (the link's file name up to its first dot):"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -E 'href="[^#"]' "$W/all-links" | sed -E 's/.*href="([^"]*)"/\1/; s#.*/##; s/[.].*//' | sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /' || :
    items_ok() { [ "$nitems" != error ] && [ "$nanchors" != error ] && [ "$nitems" -ge 1 ] && [ "$((nitems + nanchors))" = "$nlinks" ]; }
    note "the index's item links were counted, the anchors excluded, and the two account for every link (change L40)" "$(is items_ok)"
    printf '<li><a href="#structs">S</a></li><li><a href="#enums">E</a></li>\n<li><a href="struct.A.html">A</a></li>\n<li><a href="sub/enum.B.html">B</a></li>\n<li><a href="fn.c.html">c</a></li>\n' >"$W/c-all.html"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E '<li><a href="[^"]*"' "$W/c-all.html" >"$W/c-all-links"
    ctl "item links in a planted index of three items and two anchors, same command form" 3 count_matches -E 'href="[^#"]' "$W/c-all-links"
    ctl "section anchors in the same planted index, same command form" 2 count_matches -E 'href="#' "$W/c-all-links"
    # Change G36, kept: the probe crate's feature sets as part 6 P4 left them,
    # copy and copy with comments among them (the phase adds no probe).
    for pf in emend,xml dates rowcol metadata rules tables comments images richtext comments,richtext sheetprops metadata,sheetprops read copy copy,comments; do
      LINT_SHOWN="CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main cargo clippy -p size-probe --all-targets --features $pf -- -D warnings"
      lint_run "clippy, the probe crate, features $pf" "$PROBE_TARGET" cargo clippy -p size-probe --all-targets --features "$pf" -- -D warnings
    done
    printf 'warning: unused variable: `x`\nerror[E0425]: cannot find value\n    Checking emend v0.1.0\nnote: warning is not at the start\n' >"$W/c-diag"
    ctl "diag_lines over two diagnostics and two other lines, same command form" 2 diag_lines "$W/c-diag"
    
    echo
    echo "## the crate's tests with the features off, comments alone, copy alone, copy with comments and every feature, both targets (changes G24, G25, G26, G28, G29, G30, G31, G33, G34 and G35)"
    # The workspace build above turns `copy` on through the tool's dependency
    # (features unify across the workspace), so the crate alone is built here with
    # the feature off and on, into the main tree's target directory (change K35).
    passed_sum() { awk '/^test result: /{ for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^passed;?$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    failed_sum() { awk '/^test result: /{ for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^failed;?$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    ran_clean() { [ "$1" = 0 ] && [ "$2" = 0 ] && [ "$3" -gt 0 ]; }
    for target in host i686; do
      for feat in off cm on pair all; do
        args=(test -p emend)
        [ "$target" = i686 ] && args+=(--target i686-unknown-linux-musl)
        case $feat in
          cm) args+=(--features comments) ;;
          on) args+=(--features copy) ;;
          pair) args+=(--features copy,comments) ;;
          all) args+=(--all-features) ;;
        esac
        echo "command: CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main cargo ${args[*]}"
        ( cd "$MAIN" && RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$FEAT_TARGET cargo "${args[@]}" ) >"$W/t-$target-$feat.out" 2>"$W/t-$target-$feat.err"
        rc=$?
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -E '^test result: ' "$W/t-$target-$feat.out" | sed 's/^/    /'
        p=$(passed_sum "$W/t-$target-$feat.out"); fl=$(failed_sum "$W/t-$target-$feat.out")
        echo "  $target, feature $feat: exit $rc; passed $p; failed $fl"
        printf -v "P_${target}_${feat}" '%s' "$p"
        note "the crate's tests pass on $target with the feature $feat, some run and none failed" "$(is ran_clean "$rc" "$fl" "$p")"
      done
    done
    echo "  passed: host off $P_host_off, host cm $P_host_cm, host on $P_host_on, host pair $P_host_pair, host all $P_host_all, i686 off $P_i686_off, i686 cm $P_i686_cm, i686 on $P_i686_on, i686 pair $P_i686_pair, i686 all $P_i686_all (cm: comments alone; on: copy alone; pair: copy and comments; all: every feature)"
    note "the host and i686 run the same tests with the feature off" "$(is [ "$P_host_off" = "$P_i686_off" ])"
    note "the host and i686 run the same tests with comments alone" "$(is [ "$P_host_cm" = "$P_i686_cm" ])"
    note "the host and i686 run the same tests with copy alone (change G35)" "$(is [ "$P_host_on" = "$P_i686_on" ])"
    note "the host and i686 run the same tests with copy and comments" "$(is [ "$P_host_pair" = "$P_i686_pair" ])"
    note "the host and i686 run the same tests with every feature (change G35)" "$(is [ "$P_host_all" = "$P_i686_all" ])"
    note "with comments alone more tests run than with the features off, on the host" "$(is [ "$P_host_cm" -gt "$P_host_off" ])"
    note "with copy alone more tests run than with the features off, on the host" "$(is [ "$P_host_on" -gt "$P_host_off" ])"
    note "with copy alone more tests run than with the features off, on i686" "$(is [ "$P_i686_on" -gt "$P_i686_off" ])"
    note "with copy and comments more tests run than with copy alone, on the host" "$(is [ "$P_host_pair" -gt "$P_host_on" ])"
    note "with copy and comments more tests run than with comments alone, on the host" "$(is [ "$P_host_pair" -gt "$P_host_cm" ])"
    note "with every feature more tests run than with copy and comments, on the host (change G35)" "$(is [ "$P_host_all" -gt "$P_host_pair" ])"
    printf 'test result: ok. 7 passed; 1 failed; 2 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out\ntest result: ok. 3 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored\n' >"$W/c-results"
    ctl "passed_sum over two result lines, same command form" 10 passed_sum "$W/c-results"
    ctl "failed_sum over the same lines, same command form" 1 failed_sum "$W/c-results"
    
    echo
    echo "## the consumer crate naming the call the feature copy adds, with the features off, comments alone, copy alone and the two together (part 4a P1's change G3, kept; change E35)"
    mkdir -p "$CONSUMER/src" || fail=1
    {
      printf '[package]\nname = "copy-consumer"\nversion = "0.0.0"\nedition = "2024"\npublish = false\n\n'
      printf '[workspace]\n\n[dependencies]\nemend = { path = "%s" }\n\n' "$MAIN/crates/emend"
      printf '[features]\ncomments = ["emend/comments"]\ncopy = ["emend/copy"]\n'
    } >"$CONSUMER/Cargo.toml"
    cat >"$CONSUMER/src/lib.rs" <<'CONSUMER'
    //! Names, once, the call the feature `copy` adds in M3 part 6 P3
    //! (specs/0028-images-and-comments-second-half.md, "The copy").
    use std::io::Cursor;
    type P = emend::package::Package<Cursor<Vec<u8>>>;
    pub fn a(p: &mut P) -> bool { p.copy_sheet("a", "b").is_ok() }
    CONSUMER
    # The workspace's lock, so the check resolves offline to the versions the
    # workspace pins.
    cp "$MAIN/Cargo.lock" "$CONSUMER/Cargo.lock" || fail=1
    echo "  <build>/consumer/Cargo.toml:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$CONSUMER/Cargo.toml"
    echo "  <build>/consumer/src/lib.rs:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$CONSUMER/src/lib.rs"
    # Change E35: "off" the features off, "cm" comments alone, "on" copy alone,
    # "pair" copy and comments; into the consumer's own target directory (K35).
    for feat in off cm on pair; do
      args=(check --offline --message-format short)
      case $feat in
        cm) args+=(--features comments) ;;
        on) args+=(--features copy) ;;
        pair) args+=(--features copy,comments) ;;
      esac
      echo "command: (cd <build>/consumer && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/consumer cargo ${args[*]})"
      ( cd "$CONSUMER" && RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CONSUMER_TARGET cargo "${args[@]}" ) >"$W/k-$feat.out" 2>&1
      printf -v "K_RC_$feat" '%s' "$?"
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -E '(error|warning)' "$W/k-$feat.out" | sed 's/^/    /'
    done
    nerr_off=$(count_matches -E 'error\[E[0-9]+\]' "$W/k-off.out")
    nerr_cm=$(count_matches -E 'error\[E[0-9]+\]' "$W/k-cm.out")
    nerr_on=$(count_matches -E 'error' "$W/k-on.out")
    nerr_pair=$(count_matches -E 'error' "$W/k-pair.out")
    echo "  features off: exit $K_RC_off, error lines with a code $nerr_off; comments alone: exit $K_RC_cm, error lines with a code $nerr_cm; copy alone: exit $K_RC_on, lines naming an error $nerr_on; copy and comments: exit $K_RC_pair, lines naming an error $nerr_pair"
    CONSUMER_ITEMS='copy_sheet'
    names_each_once() {
      local item n
      for item in $CONSUMER_ITEMS; do
        n=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -E 'error\[E[0-9]+\]' "$1" | count_matches -F "\`$item\`" /dev/stdin)
        [ "$n" = 1 ] || return 1
      done
    }
    nitems=$(printf '%s\n' $CONSUMER_ITEMS | count_lines /dev/stdin)
    for feat in off cm; do
      case $feat in off) label="the features off" ;; cm) label="comments alone" ;; esac
      for item in $CONSUMER_ITEMS; do
        echo "  error lines naming \`$item\` with $label: $(LC_ALL=C "$G" -E 'error\[E[0-9]+\]' "$W/k-$feat.out" | count_matches -F "\`$item\`" /dev/stdin)"
      done
    done
    note "with the features off cargo check fails" "$(isnot [ "$K_RC_off" = 0 ])"
    note "with the features off there is one error line per item named ($nitems)" "$(is [ "$nerr_off" = "$nitems" ])"
    note "with the features off each item is named by exactly one error line" "$(is names_each_once "$W/k-off.out")"
    note "with comments alone cargo check fails (change E35)" "$(isnot [ "$K_RC_cm" = 0 ])"
    note "with comments alone there is one error line per item named ($nitems)" "$(is [ "$nerr_cm" = "$nitems" ])"
    note "with comments alone each item is named by exactly one error line" "$(is names_each_once "$W/k-cm.out")"
    note "control: with copy alone cargo check passes" "$(is [ "$K_RC_on" = 0 ])"
    note "control: with copy alone no line names an error" "$(is [ "$nerr_on" = 0 ])"
    note "control: with copy and comments cargo check passes" "$(is [ "$K_RC_pair" = 0 ])"
    note "control: with copy and comments no line names an error" "$(is [ "$nerr_pair" = 0 ])"
    printf 'src/lib.rs:5:35: error[E0599]: no method named `other` found\n' >"$W/c-k"
    note "control: names_each_once refuses output naming another method, not copy_sheet" "$(isnot names_each_once "$W/c-k")"
    
    echo
    echo "## status after the run, the lines printed (change K4)"
    # run_lines and run_matches read the command's own exit status. Planning's
    # spec, specs/0031, sits modified in the working tree with its rulings
    # during P1, uncommitted; that path is named and allowed (change J45). The
    # phase writes no record besides its logs.
    echo "command: git status --porcelain"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    PLAN_RE='^ M specs/0031-release-metadata[.]md$'
    st_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    st_untracked_log=$(run_matches -E '^[?][?] records/logs/m4p2-p1' git status --porcelain)
    st_tracked_log=$(run_matches -E '^ ?[MARCD] records/logs/m4p2-p1' git status --porcelain)
    st_planning=$(run_matches -E "$PLAN_RE" git status --porcelain)
    echo "status lines: $st_all; untracked under the log directory: $st_untracked_log; tracked and modified under it: $st_tracked_log; planning's spec modified and uncommitted: $st_planning"
    status_accounted() {
      [ "$st_all" != error ] && [ "$st_untracked_log" != error ] &&
        [ "$st_tracked_log" != error ] && [ "$st_planning" != error ] &&
        [ "$st_all" = "$((st_untracked_log + st_tracked_log + st_planning))" ]
    }
    note "every change in the working tree is one of this phase's logs or planning's spec" "$(is status_accounted)"
    printf '?? records/logs/m4p2-p1/gate.log\n?? records/logs/m4p1-p3/x.log\n M scripts/check.sh\n' >"$W/c-status"
    ctl "the phase's log directory in a status listing of three, same pattern" 1 count_matches -E '^[?][?] records/logs/m4p2-p1' "$W/c-status"
    printf ' M specs/0031-release-metadata.md\n M ROADMAP.md\n M specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md\n M README.md\n' >"$W/c-spec"
    ctl "planning's spec in a status listing of four, same pattern" 1 count_matches -E "$PLAN_RE" "$W/c-spec"
    echo
    echo "## this script's own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    nerr=$(wc -c <"$ERR")
    cp "$ERR" "$W/c-err"; printf 'x' >>"$W/c-err"
    nerr_ctl=$(wc -c <"$W/c-err")
    echo "  command: wc -c <phase>/out/gate.stderr: $nerr bytes; a copy with one byte appended: $nerr_ctl"
    note "this script wrote nothing to its standard error" "$(is [ "$nerr" = 0 ])"
    note "control: the same count reads one byte more in the copy" "$(is [ "$nerr_ctl" = "$((nerr + 1))" ])"
    echo "run ended at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    echo "gate log checks all as expected: $([ "$fail" -eq 0 ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    exec 1>&3
    wait "$SCRUB_PID" 2>/dev/null
    exit "$fail"

## the shared counting library this log sources
    # emend shared counting forms (specs/0007-gate-self-test.md, "scripts/counting.sh").
    #
    # Sourced by scripts/gate-self-test.sh and by the log scripts of later phases,
    # which use these instead of carrying their own copy.
    #
    # WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. In T3 P4 four counting sites compared a bare `grep -c`
    # with 0 without reading the exit status, so a read error printed 0 and the
    # check passed. Two independent checks found them, and the class was declared
    # closed three further times while instances still stood: a helper whose first
    # repair read grep's status while `cat` was the failing command, and both
    # halves of one function in T2 P7. Planning's remedy is that every counting
    # form, including a throwaway one, is a named function that reads the exit
    # status and has a positive control, from the start.
    #
    # Every function prints either a number or the word "error". None of them ever
    # prints a matched line, a value, or a path. A caller that compares a result
    # with 0 therefore cannot mistake a failed read for an absence.
    #
    # counting_controls runs every form against a match, a miss and an unreadable
    # file, prints one line per control, and sets counting_controls_ok. Callers run
    # it before using any form.
    
    G=/usr/bin/grep
    
    # count_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: total matching lines across the
    # files, or "error" if any file could not be read. The files go to grep
    # directly: with `cat file | grep -c`, an unreadable file makes CAT fail while
    # grep counts 0 over the empty stream and exits 1, so the read error reads as
    # "no hits".
    count_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_from_file <-F|-E> <pattern file> <file>...: the same, with the patterns
    # read from a file (grep -f), so a pattern is never printed.
    count_from_file() {
      local mode=$1 patterns=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -f "$patterns" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_bytes <tr class> <file>...: total bytes of that class across the files,
    # or "error" if any file could not be read. Each file is read on its own rather
    # than through `cat "$@" | tr`, for the same reason as above.
    count_bytes() {
      local class=$1 total=0 f n
      shift
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd "$class" <"$f" | wc -c) || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_lines <file>...: total lines, or "error" if any file could not be read.
    count_lines() {
      local total=0 f n
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(wc -l <"$f") || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_matches_i <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: count_matches with -i, the form
    # the hygiene step uses for OFFICE_RE and ZONE_RE. It lived in a log script as a
    # hand-rolled copy with no control of its own (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap
    # 14); a counting form belongs here, with a control, even a throwaway one.
    count_matches_i() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c -i "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # run_lines <command...>: run the command, and print the number of lines it
    # wrote on stdout, or "error" if the command itself failed. The log scripts
    # asserted a clean working tree with
    #   git status --porcelain >file 2>/dev/null || : >file
    # which turns a FAILED git status into an empty file, so the check read a
    # failed command as a clean tree (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap 1; planning
    # reproduced it). Reading the command's exit status is the whole point: a
    # command that could not run is never the same as a command that found nothing.
    run_lines() {
      local out rc
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | wc -l | tr -d ' '
    }
    
    # run_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <command...>: the same, counting only the lines
    # that match, so a caller can compare "all lines" with "lines of the expected
    # shape" without either count hiding a failed command.
    run_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" || true
    }
    
    CTRL_CLASS='\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177'
    NONASCII_CLASS='\200-\377'
    
    # counting_controls <label prefix>: run every counting form above against a
    # fixture that must match and one that must not, and against an unreadable
    # file, printing one line per result. Sets counting_controls_ok to yes or no.
    # This is the positive control planning requires for every form, and it also
    # proves each form reports "error" rather than 0 when it cannot read.
    counting_controls() {
      local d ok=yes r
      d=$(mktemp -d) || { counting_controls_ok=no; return; }
      printf 'alpha\nbeta needle gamma\nneedle\n' >"$d/hit"
      printf 'nothing of interest\n' >"$d/miss"
      printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m\017 y\ncaf\303\251\n' >"$d/bytes"
      printf 'needle\n' >"$d/patterns"
      printf 'unreadable\n' >"$d/locked"
      chmod 000 "$d/locked"
    
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit");        echo "  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/miss");       echo "  control count_matches on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_matches summed over two files: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -E 'ne+dle' "$d/hit");      echo "  control count_matches with a regular expression: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/locked");     echo "  control count_matches on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_matches on readable plus unreadable: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/hit"); echo "  control count_from_file on the same file: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_from_file on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_from_file on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/bytes");    echo "  control count_bytes, control bytes in a file with ESC, ESC and SI: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$d/bytes"); echo "  control count_bytes, non-ASCII bytes in a file with one two-byte character: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/miss");     echo "  control count_bytes on a clean file: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_bytes on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/hit");                    echo "  control count_lines on a three-line file: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/locked");                 echo "  control count_lines on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      printf 'NEEDLE\nneedle\n' >"$d/mixedcase"
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/mixedcase"); echo "  control count_matches_i on mixed case: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/mixedcase");  echo "  control count_matches on the same file, case sensitive: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_matches_i on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines printf 'a\nb\nc\n');            echo "  control run_lines on a command printing three lines: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines true);                          echo "  control run_lines on a command printing nothing: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines false);                         echo "  control run_lines on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines "$d/no-such-command");          echo "  control run_lines on a command that cannot run: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle printf 'needle\nother\n'); echo "  control run_matches on a command printing one match: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle false);             echo "  control run_matches on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
    
      chmod 644 "$d/locked"
      rm -rf "${d:?}"
      counting_controls_ok=$ok
      echo "  counting controls: $([ "$ok" = yes ] && echo "all as expected" || echo FAILED)"
    }

## counting controls
  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_matches on a file with none: 0 (expect 0)
  control count_matches summed over two files: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_matches with a regular expression: 2 (expect 2)
